+# Live path: runtime-loop transfers did not settle at standard limits
+
+Fixed in `fb9234001` (2026-10-23, branch `perf/sdk-tx-perf`). Found 2026-10-22 by the sdk-tx-perf live-limit parity
+test; it already failed at `fcbd58a09`.
+
+## Shape
+
+```
+contract C {
+    bytes32 acc;
+    function run(bytes32 seed, bytes20[] recipients, int amount) public {
+        this.acc = seed;
+        for (int i = 0; i < recipients.length; i++) {
+            this.transfer(new LockingBytecodeP2PKH(recipients[i]), amount);
+        }
+    }
+}
+```
+
+On a provider the SDK treats as live (`packages/solidcash/test/live-like-provider.ts`: no published limits, no
+simulator), the final preflight refused the first `run(...)`: `messageBus: BCH-2026 preflight failed at input 0:
+Program failed an OP_VERIFY operation.` Mocknet at relaxed limits settled it.
+
+## Cause
+
+The trace shape, not the limits or the live path as such.
+
+- The SDK starts each runtime-loop transfer at a placeholder lock (P2PKH of 20 zero bytes) and learns the real lock
+  from the probe's `OP_OUTPUTBYTECODE` check (`stateful/sc-derive-full-phase2-apply-runtime-loop.ts:103-106`).
+- That check is `2 PICK OUTPUTBYTECODE 2 PICK EQUALVERIFY` (solidc `emitRuntimeLoopEffectVerification`): the actual
+  lock below, the record's lock on top.
+- For `OP_OUTPUTBYTECODE`, `extractVerifiedValuesFromTrace` paired against the "actual" read from the state after the
+  introspection (`stateful/trace-verified-value-helpers.ts:246-248`, `:282-286`). That is right on a full trace.
+- A provider with `maximumInputBytes` of 10,000 or less gets a reduced trace (`stateful/faithful-probe-trace.ts`),
+  and a live provider defaults to 10,000. There the state after the introspection is the equality itself, whose top
+  is the expected lock, so the extractor returned the current placeholder. Nothing was learned, the next probe
+  repeated, and the final preflight failed the lock check. Both instruments reduce, so both failed.
+
+## Fix
+
+`extractVerifiedValuesFromTrace` gains `pairObservedActual` (default `true`, so other callers are unchanged), and the
+runtime-loop read passes `false`: every runtime-loop flush puts the record's lock on top, so the positional operand is
+exact on every trace shape. On a full trace the pairing already returned that operand, so relaxed mocknet bytes do
+not change.
+
+## Verification
+
+`packages/solidcash/test/e2e/LiveLimitProbeParity.test.ts`: S5 now settles on the live-like provider with identical
+bytes under the sparse observer and `debug()`, and its flow asserts the recipients and amounts each call pays. Its
+second call pays 700 satoshis: 500 is below the 546-satoshi dust threshold a live network enforces, which the relaxed
+mock does not, and the bug had hidden that.
+
+With S5 settled, the sdk-tx-perf spec retires the full-trace forcing for runtime-loop transfer probes (SPEC I2).
