+## 8. Memory and per-probe CPU
+
+### 8.1 Drop the eager discovery debug
+
+`runSendDiscoveryProbe` calls `covenantBuilder.debug()` at standard limits and then rebuilds
+(`stb-run-send-discovery-probe.ts:22,56`). Drop the `debug()` and keep the rebuild. The relaxed branch
+already skips the debug and still rebuilds, so every mocknet test exercises the post-change path; the only
+new evidence needed is **byte identity at 10k**, showing the `debug()` call does not change the builder.
+If bytes match, no "already-converged" condition is needed: nothing consumes the probe's result
+(`discoveryProbeFailure` is discarded at `StatefulTransactionBuilder.ts:7184`).
+
+Two effects must survive:
+
+- **Density limit.** The density-limit throw is the only consumed outcome. Keep it with one cheap
+  `evaluate()` per input that throws the same actionable message, or map the final preflight's density
+  failure to that message.
+- **`console.log`.** Contract logs come from the template debugger (`debugging.ts:529`). At standard
+  limits this probe is likely the only place a stateful send prints them. **Decision (confirmed): keep the `debug()` only when the covenant artifact's debug info has log
+  entries** (`artifact.debug.logs`, `debug.functionDebug[selector].logs`, `invokeDebug`; the debugger
+  reads the same three sources at `debugging.ts:325-333`). Contracts that use `console.log` keep their
+  output; contracts that do not stop paying for the trace.
+
+The plain path has the same waste: `TransactionBuilder.send()` runs `this.debug()` best-effort for every
+covenant input on every network and swallows the error (`TransactionBuilder.ts:1474`). Apply the same log
+gate there. Non-covenant standard inputs keep their full debug; P2PKH is cheap.
+
+The plain path's density check is **new behaviour**, not something preserved. Today that call swallows
+every error, including a density failure, so the refusal currently arrives from the node or the mock
+verifier. The cheap `evaluate()` turns it into an SDK error that arrives before broadcast and carries
+the salt guidance, instead of the node's or mock's generic rejection. It does **not** arrive before
+signing: `send()` calls `buildLibauthTransaction()` first (`TransactionBuilder.ts:1464`) and debugs
+after it.
+
+The covenant-branch check should throw `FailedTransactionEvaluationError`, matching the non-covenant
+branch, so the plain path reports density failures one way. `test/e2e/StatelessDensityReserve.test.ts`
+is the plain-path density test; it exercises the non-covenant branch, which keeps its full debug, so
+step 1 does not break it. `expectOverOperationCostBudget` (`test/test-util.ts:521`) is the shared helper
+several call sites use. A grep for the density message reaches 14 test files; review all of them, not a
+shortlist.
+
+### 8.2 Swap `debug()` for the faithful shallow recorder at standard limits
+
+This is the lowest-risk memory/CPU change. It is step 2, after the discovery-debug work.
+
+One constraint: `evaluateFaithfulOrDebugTrace` already picks the recorder only when
+`usesFastVmPaths(provider)` (`createVirtualMachine.ts:118`), because the recorder's phase exits come from
+`installCachedP2shEvaluator`, installed only on that path. A live provider has no `consensusLimits`, so
+step 2 must install the phase-exit hook for it (or provide an equivalent) and prove parity before
+switching the gate. Flipping the gate alone would run an incomplete recorder.
+
+Run that parity check on a **live-like** provider (`simulator = false`, no fast paths). The mock's deploy
+fixtures fail in that configuration on coin proof (`ownCoinRefusal` needs the simulator ledger), not on
+the VM path, so use a script-only harness, keep coin proof on a separate path, or use real transactions.
+Parity measured on the simulator does not cover the configuration step 2 adds.
+
+`createFaithfulTraceVmForProvider` is documented as
+`debug()`-equivalent, shares the function table, and avoids `proxyDebug`'s spread-argument limit. The
+parity harness at `faithful-probe-trace.ts:987` already compares the two when
+`useFaithfulRecorder` is true; enable that comparison at standard limits and run the derivation corpus
+before switching the gate.
+
+The sparse observer is a different instrument. The objection currently cited against it
+(`createVirtualMachine.ts:774`, phantom commitments from invisible intervening opcodes) predates
+`reduceProbeTrace`, so `debug()` has the same blind spot on the reduced path. The `ip - 1` remedy
+proposed in the first revision is wrong for the reason in §7.2. Do not build on that argument.
+
+Measure the recorder against `debug()` on a real outlined contract. The installed fork already shares
+the function table, so the expected win is smaller than the stock-libauth comment suggests.
+
+### 8.3 Lower-priority memory items
+
+| item | correction |
+|---|---|
+| Program copy per evaluation | Only runs that stop on a recorded close copy the program (`createVirtualMachine.ts:1213`). Measure its share before changing it. |
+| Hex fixed-point sets | Relay-standard transactions are at most ~100 KB, so the retained hex is modest; the 1.3 MB case is mock-only. Keep for the mock/bench, not the primary list. |
+| `buildBytes()` | Useful, small, independent. |
+| Unlocker argument prefix | The redeem push is already cached even with signatures (`Contract.ts:886`); only the argument prefix is re-encoded. Small. |
+| Eager discovery debug | Keep as a candidate. The code comment at `stb-run-send-discovery-probe.ts:51` claims the rebuild depends on what the probe finds; that was not verified here. Gate any removal on byte identity at production limits. |
