+# SDK transaction building and derivation: implementation spec (one goal)
+
+**Status:** implementable spec, 2026-10-22, written against `fcbd58a09` (branch `perf/sdk-tx-perf`). Revised the same
+day after review: the composer twin runs on every network (F10), data signatures stay memoizable (F11), value pins
+land with the collector (C3), the collector VM refuses reentry (C4), L1 is applied to every loop and has edge tests,
+and byte identity is checked against the base commit only (B1-B4). A second review added the F10 carve-out to
+invariant 1 and acceptance 4, memo clones (F12), the outpoint-counter reset and field-named counter comparisons
+(B3, B4), and wall time (acceptance 5). An implementability pass then settled what the reviews left open: the
+faithful trace and the first-write boundary behind L1's progress guarantee (L3), the send-side assertion after the
+final preflight (L5), the framed speculation rule with its rewind (framed 3.0) and the hop loops (framed 3.3b, F2).
+Its verification rounds added `requireConfirmedValues` and F13: a pass confirms only the values it compared.
+**Supersedes:** the step plan in `DESIGN.md` sections 11-12. `DESIGN.md` keeps the history, the prior art (relaxed
+discovery, removed in `8d335f51f`) and the measurements this spec relies on. Where the two disagree, this spec wins,
+notably over DESIGN 7.4's clean probe on loop exit (replaced by L1) and DESIGN 8.2's recorder at standard limits
+(replaced by the sparse observer at every limit).
+**Progress:** commit 1 (instruments) has landed (`4ef7d7f31`). The live runtime-loop transfer bug S5 had pinned is
+fixed (`fb9234001`), and S5 is a byte-identity case. The next commit is 2.
+**Shape:** one goal. Every part lands on this branch in the order of section 6, each commit with its own tests. Byte
+identity and the full ladder run once, at the end (section 7). No part waits on another part's measurement.
+**Component specs** (file:line for every change, code shapes, failure behaviour, tests):
+
+| part | spec |
+|---|---|
+| probe instruments | [`spec/instruments.md`](spec/instruments.md) |
+| collector probe (suppression, pairing, authentication) | [`spec/collector-probe.md`](spec/collector-probe.md) |
+| stateful loops, ownership, provisional mark | [`spec/loops.md`](spec/loops.md) |
+| send path and builder boundary | [`spec/send-path.md`](spec/send-path.md) |
+| framed composer: batching, read-field memo, structural recipe | [`spec/framed.md`](spec/framed.md) |
+
+Where a component spec and section 4 disagree, section 4 wins. Section 4 also answers every open question the
+component specs end with. Paths are relative to `packages/solidcash/src` unless they start with `test/`.
+
+---
+
+## 1. What changes
+
+| area | today | after this goal |
+|---|---|---|
+| derivation probes | libauth `debug()` (every state cloned) on live networks; the sparse observer on mocknet | the sparse observer on every network; the faithful shallow recorder, with a phase-exit hook, wherever a full trace is needed; `debug()` only for user debugging, the override switches, and sends whose contract prints logs |
+| learning computed values | one value per probe in six loops: stateful phase 2, phase-1 entries, cleaned rescan, final repair, deploy, framed composer | one probe per dependency layer: authenticated failed checks are suppressed and recorded; a run that suppresses nothing is the verdict |
+| stateful send | an eager `debug()` of the whole transaction on every standard-limit send, result discarded (about 240 ms per send in the measured file) | the template debug only when the contract has `console.log` entries; a cheap per-input density check keeps the actionable refusal |
+| plain covenant send | a swallowed best-effort `debug()` on every network | the same log gate plus the density check |
+| framed composer | each attempt re-walks and re-evaluates every master; on live networks every read is a full `debug()` | on every network: batched walks, an exact read-field memo for walks and evaluations, and a structural recipe for the walks the memo cannot prove |
+| builder boundary | hex round trips; hex fixed-point sets | `buildBytes()`; a hashed fixed-point set |
+
+## 2. Why this shape
+
+- **Where the time is** (`DESIGN.md` 5.3). On the production probe path the eager discovery `debug()` was 4.79 s of
+  a 4.75 s slowdown over 20 sends; phase-2 probing was 3-13% of test time; the framed composer is the largest
+  absolute cost (`take job`: 61 s, 1,014 evaluations and 274 walks).
+- **One instrument closes the mocknet/live split.** Mocknet derived with the sparse observer and live networks with
+  `debug()`, so the mocknet suite never tested the live path, and that split hid live-only failures before
+  (2026-08-05). After this goal the two differ only in limits, in the stateful lane and in the framed composer
+  (F10). The objection recorded against the observer at
+  standard limits (`network/createVirtualMachine.ts:774`, "phantom commitments") predates `reduceProbeTrace`, which
+  makes the `debug()` path equally blind to unobserved opcodes; `spec/instruments.md` section 9 gives the
+  equivalence analysis.
+- **Batching never loses ground.** A suppressing run's first suppressed check is where a clean run stops, and its
+  value does not depend on anything suppressed, so a suppressing run learns at least what a clean run learns.
+- **The memo is exact.** VM evaluation is deterministic in what it reads, so reusing a verdict when every read
+  field is byte-equal is sound by construction; no heuristic decides it.
+
+## 3. Parts
+
+### 3.1 Probe instruments (`spec/instruments.md`)
+
+- Change A: a phase-exit-only hook wraps the per-phase evaluate callback of libauth's own `instructionSet.evaluate`
+  (where `debug()` records phase ends). Installed only on recorder VMs without the cached P2SH evaluator, so live
+  providers get a recorder equal to `debug()` state for state.
+- Change B: `installSparseProbeBranchSkips` moves out of the fast-path block (`:923-1099`), so every sparse
+  observer skips inactive branches. Hardened for the 2026 instruction set: a conditional with a second `OP_ELSE`, or
+  one a loop crosses, gets no skip target, and a skip that would hide a control-stack depth failure steps instead.
+  (An earlier draft listed `OP_VERIF`, `OP_VERNOTIF`, `OP_2MUL` and `OP_2DIV`; those fail unexecuted only in 2023.)
+- Change C: exported `ProbeOperationWrapper` and `ProviderVmObserver`. `createFaithfulTraceVmForProvider` keeps its
+  signature: with C1 no recorder suppresses.
+- Change D: `evaluateProbeTrace` defaults to the sparse observer at every limit; `forceFullDebug` uses the recorder
+  (reduced at or below 10,000 bytes, whole above, as today); the override switches keep selecting `debug()`.
+- Change E: `evaluateFaithfulOrDebugTrace` drops the `usesFastVmPaths` gate (recorder everywhere).
+- Change F: the sparse collector drops states inside an inactive branch.
+- Change G: `SOLIDC_DEBUG_TRACE_PARITY=1` compares recorder vs `debug()` state for state and sparse vs a replay of
+  `debug()`'s executed states through a fresh collector; an opt-in test sink hands both to tests.
+- Change H (trimmed by C1 below): the collector's own cached sparse VM with a per-evaluation operation slot.
+- Change I: bounded candidates on live providers match mock (three phase exits). Change J: deploy derivation probes
+  sparse at every limit. Change K: comments and `docs/kernel-diagnostics.md`.
+
+### 3.2 Collector probe (`spec/collector-probe.md`)
+
+`evaluateCollectorProbe(provider, program, session)` and `createCollectorHooks(session)`. They suppress a failed
+`OP_EQUALVERIFY` only when the consuming extractor pairs it with a pending output introspection, one operand equals
+the transaction's current value at that output, and the session owns the output. They return the sparse trace plus
+records, `suppressedNothing`, `passed`, `firstSuppressedTraceIndex`, a candidate fingerprint and the faithful trace:
+what a clean run of the same transaction returns, kept at the first suppression. Shared pairing classes drive both
+the online rule and the extractors, so the rule cannot be looser than what the extractors read.
+
+### 3.3 Stateful loops (`spec/loops.md`)
+
+A shared `stateful/collector-loop.ts` drives phase 2, the cleaned rescan, phase-1 progressive entries and the deploy
+loop. The final repair suppresses through hooks on its own observer VM. Every exit is evaluated on a run that
+suppressed nothing. A suppressing run's extractors keep today's rule over the faithful prefix, and its stack-scan
+readers read the faithful trace, so it learns at least what a clean run would. Ownership is decided by type on the
+built probe: a non-minting NFT of a category the builder settles, never an `addOutput()` object or an SCID identity.
+A per-input provisional mark is asserted at `buildFinalized` and `STB.send()`. Speculative chunk growth is
+reconnected to "this run suppressed something". Nested probes, phase-1 one-shot probes and the optimistic permutation
+trials stay faithful.
+
+### 3.4 Send path and builder boundary (`spec/send-path.md`)
+
+`artifactHasDebugLogs` / `TransactionBuilder.hasDebugLogs()` gate the template debug on both send paths;
+`TransactionBuilder.assertOperationCostDensity()` throws `FailedTransactionEvaluationError` with the salt guidance
+on both. `buildBytes()` with five internal consumers switched. The progressive-entry fixed-point keys become
+`binToHex(sha256(encodeTransaction(tx)))` in commit 3, which rewrites that loop (send-path section 6).
+
+### 3.5 Framed composer (`spec/framed.md`)
+
+`boundedWalk(program, options?)` with a per-call `authenticate` predicate; `readComputedDeclarations` (the singular
+reader becomes its `.end`, so its ten callers are unchanged). `learnComputedValues` learns the first close as today
+and later distinctive closes as provisional. `call.ts`, `genesis.ts` and the hop loops batch under a speculation
+snapshot that is restored, with the attempt index, before any terminal action a passing faithful run did not justify
+(framed 3.0). The composer runs on a private VM twin,
+built on every provider (F10), that carries the read-field memo. A structural recipe adds two verified call-site
+skips. Counters split `tracedCloses` and attribute evaluations.
+
