+
+### Loops
+
+- **L1** (loops Q6). No separate suppressed-run budget. Every run counts against the loop's existing bound, so the
+  published ceilings hold, including `messageBus.resourceBudgets.maximumSemanticDerivationPasses`
+  (`message-bus/semantic-derivation-budget.ts:10`, at least 2 per participant). When one run of the bound remains,
+  it is forced clean, so every loop still ends on a clean run. This is safe because of the progress guarantee (L3,
+  loops decisions 7 and 8): a suppressing run learns at least what a clean run of the same transaction learns, with
+  the same values. Its extraction keeps today's rule over the faithful prefix, and its stack-scan readers read the
+  faithful trace. Its further values can be wrong, and the next run re-learns them. A suppressing run that learns
+  nothing new repeats its candidate, which then runs clean (loops decision 3). No apply step asserts progress: an
+  output no extractor learns, such as a callee's NFT the root pins (loops 3.2), yields nothing in either run.
+  - API: `createCollectorLoop({ eligible })` loses `maxSuppressedRuns`. `admit` and `mode` take `lastRun`, which
+    each loop computes from its own bound and which forces 'clean'.
+  - Loop caps stay today's (no `+ suppressedRuns`). The final repair counts suppressing repairs in
+    `repairsRemaining` and suppressing sweeps against `repairPassLimit`. The exception fallback's clean run is its
+    iteration's run (loops 5.6). Loops sections 2, 5-9 are written this way.
+  - Edge tests (loops 12.1 test 6, 12.3 test 17). With a bound of 2, the published minimum, and one layer of pins,
+    the loop runs suppress then clean and settles. With a bound of 2 and two layers, the cap is reached on a clean
+    run. With a bound of 1, the only run is clean. Each outcome is the base's at the same bound, or better.
+- **L2** (loops Q9). The per-input mark (`'root'` / `group:<i>`) replaces the plain boolean API.
+- **L3** (loops Q8). First write wins only past the faithful prefix. Every extraction site of a suppressing run
+  passes the prefix length as `firstWriteWins`, now `boolean | number` (loops 5.4). Observations in the prefix keep
+  today's last-write rule, so a preserve pin followed by a write at the same output keeps the write, as a clean run
+  does; past the prefix an output already learned keeps its value.
+- **L4** (loops Q7). No new growth limit. The existing region maxima (`MAX_SPECULATIVE_CHUNK_OUTPUTS` and the
+  others) apply to every run, and a repeated candidate turns suppression off.
+- **L5** (loops Q4). If `stb.build()` throws after a suppressing run while the loop's bound allows another run,
+  suppression turns off and the loop continues (loops decision 9 and 5.6). The retry builds from the same state, so a
+  provisional value that broke the layout throws again, and the error propagates; nothing is restored. In a loop's
+  last iteration, and in the cleaned rescan, whose build precedes its `try`, the error propagates at once.
+  - At finalization `STB.send()` asserts the mark after the final preflight and repair, so a failing preflight reports
+    its own error. `buildFinalized` asserts first.
+  - The assertion is an internal invariant: every path that could leave the mark set propagates an exception first.
+- **L6.** `SOLIDC_FAITHFUL_DERIVATION=1` (opt-in) restores today's one-value loops. It is a temporary development
+  oracle (B2); no committed test uses it.
