+## 5. Invariants (whole goal)
+
+1. Every transaction the base (`fcbd58a09`) produces is byte-identical after this goal, on the derivation corpus at
+   the relaxed and 10k profiles and on the marketplace fixture's broadcasts. A shape the base failed to derive at
+   10k and that now derives is recorded as a fix, not a mismatch. On a provider without published limits, F10
+   changes one reading on purpose: a walk ending at a phase-level failure reads `no-trace`. A live shape whose bytes
+   change through that reading is a fix, established explicitly by acceptance 4, not a mismatch.
+2. The final preflight (`assertFinalizedTransactionCovenants`), the mock verifier and every consensus VM are built
+   without any probe wrapper. Trace-only counters, such as the verify counter on the mock verifier's VM, are not
+   probe wrappers: they change no result.
+3. A suppressing run is never a verdict and never ends a loop. Every loop's last run suppresses nothing.
+4. Suppression applies only as section 3.2 states. Never after `OP_INPUTBYTECODE`, never for token categories, never
+   on a full-trace caller.
+5. A suppressing run learns at least what a clean run of the same transaction learns, with the same values (L1, L3).
+6. The provisional mark (per input) is clear at every finalization; `buildFinalized` and `STB.send()` assert it.
+7. Selection is by type, coordinate, effect or metadata, never by contract, function or event name.
+8. A memo hit requires byte equality of every read field plus the run's own unlocking and locking bytecode. A run
+   that checks a transaction signature hashes the signing serialization, so it is never memoized. A data signature
+   check reads only stack operands, which the key determines (F11).
+9. Values are never cached across calls; the recipe stores structure only.
+10. The composer twin evaluates as its base does on every provider: stock operations, read-only observers, no branch
+    skips (F10).
+11. The collector VM runs one evaluation at a time (C4).
