+## 8. Risks and where each is caught
+
+| risk | caught by |
+|---|---|
+| The observer at standard limits derives differently from `debug()` | parity replay (Change G), the standing cross-limit test, byte identity at 10k |
+| A suppressed failure was genuine | authentication (value plus ownership); the clean final run; the final preflight |
+| A wrong candidate from a value-dependent check | a later run re-learns it (the output stays owned); first write wins past the prefix; the progress guarantee |
+| A stack-scan reader takes a placeholder-derived item past the first failure | readers read the faithful trace, the clean run's own (loops decision 8; collector test 15) |
+| A provisional value breaks the layout and a build throws | one retry with suppression off, then the error propagates (L5); byte identity against the base (acceptance 4) |
+| The online rule drifts from the extractors | shared pairing classes; pairing-equivalence test (collector test 10) |
+| A loop exits provisional | exits only on clean runs (L1); mark assertions at `buildFinalized` and `STB.send()` |
+| Published pass ceilings exceeded | L1 single budget |
+| Framed batching changes a decision | speculation snapshot restored, with the attempt index, before any exit a passing run did not confirm, on any error and at exhaustion (framed 3.0); byte identity against the base fixtures (B4) |
+| Memo reuse when a read field changed | exactness by construction; transaction signature checks are never memoized (F11); memo unit tests |
+| The live composer reads a stop differently from `debug()` | only at phase-level failures, where it now reads as mocknet does (F10); `phaseStopWalks` and the explicit live comparison (acceptance 4); framed tests 7.1.7 and 7.2.4 |
+| A memo hit returns state a caller mutated | clones on store and on hit (F12); memo test 7.3.8 |
+| A nested collector evaluation corrupts the slot or the trace | reentry guard (C4); collector test 13 |
+| A fixture differs only because a random draw or the outpoint counter moved | seeded generator, counter reset and self-contained fixture tests (B3); draw count in every fixture; the development oracles until commit 7 |
+| A counter comparison fails on the schema change | assertions name fields both sides have (B4) |
+| A per-walk or per-evaluation cost regresses while counts improve | wall time in a clean environment (acceptance 5) |
+| A different trace window changes a derived callee return on live | S6 in the live-limit parity test: final bytes against `debug()`, with a precondition that the window holds inactive observations (instruments 12.3) |
+| A recipe skip that was wrong | the post-fill run verifies every skip; a deviation undoes and replays |
+| `console.log` output lost | the log gate reads the same sources the printer reads (send D1) |
