+# Spec: framed composer batching, read-field memo, structural recipe (DESIGN step 4, section 7.6)
+
+> Component spec of [`../SPEC.md`](../SPEC.md), the one-goal implementation spec. Where this file and SPEC.md
+> section 4 disagree, SPEC.md wins, and SPEC.md section 4 answers this file's open questions. Written read-only
+> against `fcbd58a09`; "steps" and "the coordinator" refer to the planning that produced it.
+
+Worktree `/Code/cashscript/.worktrees/sdk-tx-perf` at `fcbd58a09`, read-only. Source paths are relative to
+`packages/solidcash/src` unless they say otherwise. Line numbers are at `fcbd58a09`.
+
+## 0. Scope, decisions, findings
+
+### 0.1 Decisions
+
+- D1. `boundedDebug` becomes a wrapper of a new `boundedWalk(program, options?)`, in the same block of
+  `network/createVirtualMachine.ts`. Suppression is a per-call option of that walk. Nothing is added to an instruction
+  set. Faithful callers pass no options, so they are unchanged.
+- D2. `readComputedDeclarations` (plural) is the only reader. `readComputedDeclaration` (singular) becomes
+  `readComputedDeclarations(...).end` with no `authenticate`, which gives the same answer as today. Its ten call
+  sites stay as they are.
+- D3. The composer (`learnComputedValues`) batches. The first close of a walk is learned as today. A distinctive
+  value (at least 20 bytes) from a later close is provisional. It is settled before its learning call returns: kept
+  if the call's last, faithful walk compared it, put back to its placeholder otherwise (sections 2.2, 3.0).
+- D4. call.ts batches the root's own values under section 3.0's rule. A speculation snapshot is taken at the
+  start of the attempt whose walk first speculates. Before any terminal action a confirming run did not justify, on a
+  pass that did not compare every speculative value, on any error, and at exhaustion, the snapshot is restored with
+  its attempt index and batching is turned off.
+  Batching then speeds up the success path and can never change a decision. Payees stay singular.
+- D5. genesis.ts and proxy/deploy.ts's two hop loops batch under the same rule (sections 3.2 and 3.3b, SPEC F2).
+  proxy/deploy.ts also changes its machine (D6) and its finalization assertion.
+- D6. The composer runs on a private twin of the provider machine, built on every provider (SPEC F10). The twin has
+  a read-only observer on the introspection and transaction-signature opcodes, steps inactive branches, and is cached
+  per base VM. The provider's shared VM gets nothing new except a trace-only `verify` counter. The twin is where the
+  read-field memo lives, and it replaces copy-plus-compare for composer programs (item 6).
+- D7. The read-field rule ("run a contract only when a field it reads changed", for walks and evaluations) is an
+  exact memo. A run's verdict is reused only when the program holds the same bytes in every field that run read, plus
+  its own unlocking bytecode and its own locking bytecode. Execution is deterministic in what it reads, so this is
+  sound by construction and does not need the recipe.
+- D8. The structural recipe (key: code digest, entry, argument shape, plan/layout signature; no values) adds the two
+  skips the memo cannot prove. Both happen only at call-site fills: the learning walk where the recipe expects
+  nothing, and the confirming walk after the last expected layer. Each skip is verified in the same host step by the
+  post-fill run. A deviation undoes the fill and replays the step as it always ran. The recipe never skips an
+  evaluation.
+- D9. Item 6: no revision or digest is threaded through `programOf`. The twin keeps no program copy and does no
+  `samePlainData`. The memo snapshots only the fields a run read. The shared VMs keep today's copy-plus-compare for
+  non-composer readers, and new counters size it.
+
+### 0.2 Findings that shape the design (from the code)
+
+- F1. `verify` bypasses the evaluate wrapper. In libauth `virtual-machine.js:146-150`, `verify` closes over the inner
+  `evaluate`, and `createVirtualMachine.ts:1294` only replaces the `machine.evaluate` property. The mock verifier
+  (`network/createPreparedTxVerifier.ts:65,172`, `vm.verify(resolved)`) is therefore counted in `phaseRuns` and never
+  in `evaluations`. DESIGN 7.6 and the step-4 sizing bullet in 11 say the mock verifier is in `evaluations`; correct
+  both.
+- F2. A failed `OP_EQUALVERIFY` can be stepped past in the manual loop:
+  - `opVerify` pops the result before `applyError` (`flow-control.js:4-6`), so the stack is the one a passing close
+    leaves.
+  - `applyError` returns a fresh `{...state, error}` (`errors.js:97-100`).
+  - The error is exactly `AuthenticationErrorCommon.failedVerify` (`format/error.js:33-34`; an empty stack gives a
+    different error).
+  - `continue` stops only on `error !== undefined` (`bch-2026-instruction-set.js:34-45`).
+
+  The metrics differ by one pushed byte per suppressed close (OP_EQUAL pushes an empty item, not `0x01`). A
+  suppressing walk is therefore never a verdict.
+- F3. `OP_INVOKE` swaps `state.instructions` in place (`createVirtualMachine.ts:411-417`), and a function returns
+  inside `continue`. Every close in an outlined function is a step of the walk.
+- F4. 739 test call sites pass `vm: compositionMachine()`, the provider's cached observerless VM
+  (`solidc/test/framed/machine.ts:35-38`). `call.ts:988` uses the same cache, as does the final verifier. Anything
+  installed on that VM leaks into every caller.
+- F5. Typed-call value closes (`call.ts:2771-2789`) match `computed == recordValueBytes(0n)`, which is not a
+  sentinel, so they are never authenticated. Their operand widths and values (`(h)`: an 8-byte declared value and a zero
+  computed value) are disjoint from `(g)` (non-zero 8-byte sentinel) and `(i)` (4-5 byte sentinel). Evaluating `(h)`
+  after `(i)` therefore changes no outcome.
+- F6. Record commitments and witnesses can be 1-2 bytes, so "operand equals a learned value" can collide with
+  unrelated checks. Placeholders (`draft.ts:150-153`, sha256) and the call.ts sentinels (`call.ts:296,395,1689-1781`)
+  are distinctive.
+- F7. Precedent for read recording: `message-bus/preflight.ts:3055-3087` observes reads with an inactive-branch skip
+  (`controlStack.some((frame) => frame === false)`) and treats an index it cannot name conservatively.
+- F8. Side finding, out of scope: `proxy/deploy.ts:2289` labels `0xb0`/`0xb1` as CHECKSIG/CHECKSIGVERIFY. They
+  are OP_NOP1/OP_CHECKLOCKTIMEVERIFY. It is a trace label only.
