+### 1.2 `framed/deploy/declaration.ts`
+
+Restructure the 140-line file:
+
+- `:39-46` `BoundedDebugVirtualMachine` gains `boundedWalk?: (program, options?) => BoundedWalk<ProgramStateTrace>`.
+- Extract `:92-103` unchanged into `readingOfTrace(trace, maximumCommitmentBytes): DeclarationReading`. Also extract
+  `stopOfTrace(trace): RunStop`, the same classification without the plausibility bound, so the memo can store it once
+  and each caller can apply its own bound. `RunStop` is defined in `framed/composer/run-memo.ts` (section 5.1):
+  `{ kind: 'passed' } | { kind: 'close'; close: ReadDeclaration } | { kind: 'other'; reading: DeclarationReading }`.
+  `readingOfStop(stop, bound)` maps `'close'` through `closeReading`, returns `'other'` as it is, and maps `'passed'`
+  to `{ ok: false, reason: 'no-trace', error: undefined }`, today's reading of a passed run (`:92-93`). A passed walk
+  has no failed stepped state, so `stopOfTrace` never returns `'passed'`; step 6 below stores it from `passed`.
+- Export `closeReading` (`:107`) for `rootLearningOf` (section 3.1).
+- New API:
+
+```ts
+/** Every close a run reached that the caller can learn from, and how the run ended. */
+export interface ComputedDeclarations {
+  /** The failed closes the walk stepped past because the caller authenticated them, in run order. */
+  readonly closes: readonly ReadDeclaration[];
+  /** The run's stop read as `readComputedDeclaration` reads it; the faithful reading only when `closes` is empty. */
+  readonly end: DeclarationReading;
+  /** True when the run passed every check; faithful only when `closes` is empty. */
+  readonly passed: boolean;
+  readonly source: 'walk' | 'trace' | 'recorded' | 'memo';
+}
+
+export function readComputedDeclarations(options: {
+  readonly vm: VirtualMachine;
+  readonly program: VirtualMachineProgram;
+  readonly maximumCommitmentBytes: number;
+  /** A failed close this accepts is learned and walked past. Absent: the faithful reading, as today. */
+  readonly authenticate?: (close: ReadDeclaration) => boolean;
+  readonly maximumSuppressed?: number;
+  /** Passed to the walk (1.1). A read with it always walks: steps 2 and 3 have no closes to report. */
+  readonly notePassed?: (value: Uint8Array) => void;
+}): ComputedDeclarations;
+```
+
+Logic, in this order:
+
+1. `bumpFramedCounter('declarationReads')`.
+2. Unless `notePassed` is given, if `composerMemoOf(vm)` (section 5.1) has a verdict for `program`:
+   - Answer `{ closes: [], end: readingOfStop(stop, bound), passed, source: 'memo' }` and bump `memoReadHits`.
+   - Exception: when the stop is `'close'` and `authenticate?.(stop.close)` is true, a walk must collect the later
+     closes, so fall through.
+3. Unless `notePassed` is given, if `machine.recordedClose?.(program)` returns a close and `authenticate` does not
+   accept it, answer as today:
+   `recordedCloses` and `closeReading(recorded, bound)`, `passed: false`, `source: 'recorded'`. An accepted recorded
+   close falls through to the walk, which reaches it again and goes on.
+4. `bumpFramedCounter('tracedCloses')`.
+   - With `machine.boundedWalk`: walk with `{ authenticate: authenticate && ((d, c) => authenticate({ declared: d,
+     computed: c })), maximumSuppressed, notePassed }`. `states = walk.states`, `passed = vm.stateSuccess(walk.final)
+     === true`.
+   - Otherwise: `trace = vm.debug(program)` with no suppression; `passed` is `stateSuccess` of the trace's last element.
+     Only a machine without `boundedWalk` gets here (a stock libauth VM or an observer VM a caller hands in). The twin
+     has `boundedWalk` on every provider (SPEC F10). This path notes nothing, so it confirms nothing (section 3.0).
+5. `end = readingOfTrace(states, bound)`.
+6. If the machine is a composer twin and `walk.suppressed.length === 0`, call `memo.note(program, walk.reads,
+   { final: walk.final, passed, stop: passed ? { kind: 'passed' } : stopOfTrace(states) })`.
+7. Counter split (section 4): `suppressedCloses += closes.length`, then:
+   - No `authenticate`: `tracedPassed` when passed; `tracedUnclassified` when `end.ok || end.close` (a readable close
+     the caller judges); `tracedNothing` otherwise.
+   - With `authenticate`: `tracedLearned` when closes are non-empty; `tracedPassed` when passed; `tracedNothing`
+     otherwise.
+8. Return `{ closes: walk.suppressed, end, passed, source: 'walk' | 'trace' }`.
+
+`readComputedDeclaration(options)` becomes `readComputedDeclarations(options).end`. `declaresCommitment` and
+`eventCloseOf` are unchanged.
+
+### 1.3 Invariants and failure behavior
+
+- With no `authenticate`, every answer equals today's: the same stop, reason, opcode and operands. The memo answers only
+  in the exact cases listed in section 5.1.
+- An unauthenticated failure always ends the walk. So do a non-EQUALVERIFY error, an empty-stack EQUALVERIFY, and a
+  limit error, because the error string differs. A suppressing walk's `end` and `passed` are never used as a verdict
+  (D3, D4, D5).
+- The first entry of `closes` is the walk's first failure. Every earlier failure would have been unauthenticated, and
+  that would have ended the walk.
+- Hitting the bound ends the walk on the next authenticated failure as a faithful stop.
