+### 3.2 `framed/deploy/genesis.ts`
+
+**`:1262`.** `const vm = composerMachineOf(createVirtualMachineBch2026ForProvider(options.provider));`
+
+**Extract the matcher.** `learnDeclaration` (`:1447-1488`) splits into:
+- `genesisLearningOf(close, state)`, which matches in the same order: skipped emit, witness, record, reached
+  emit, node;
+- the application, unchanged.
+
+The matching is against the current `records`, `events` and `nodes`, so it is already re-learnable.
+
+**Loop (`:1312-1331`).** Section 3.0 applies. The learned state is `viewOuts`, `eventOuts`, `nodeOuts` and
+`settledSideCars`, rebound at `:1329-1332` and unchanged between an iteration's start and its walk, so `origin` is
+taken at the walk. In genesis a confirming walk accepts and ends the loop, so `pending` is `origin !== undefined`.
+
+```ts
+let origin: { readonly state: GenesisLearned; readonly iteration: number } | undefined;
+const speculative = new Map<string, Uint8Array>();   // by slot: record:i, event:i, node:i, side-car id
+let batching = !framedLegacyEnabled();
+for (let iteration = 0; ; iteration += 1) {
+  if (iteration >= maximumIterations && origin === undefined) break;
+  let restore = iteration >= maximumIterations;          // exhaustion with origin set
+  if (!restore) {
+    try {
+      const program = build(viewOuts, eventOuts, nodeOuts, settledSideCars);
+      const passed = new Set<string>();
+      const read = readComputedDeclarations({ vm, program, maximumCommitmentBytes: readingBound,
+        ...(batching && iteration < maximumIterations - 1
+          ? { authenticate: (close: ReadDeclaration): boolean => genesisLearningOf(close, learnedNow()) !== undefined }
+          : {}),
+        ...(origin !== undefined ? { notePassed: (value: Uint8Array): void => { passed.add(bytesToHex(value)); } }
+          : {}) });
+      if (read.closes.length > 0) {
+        if (read.closes.some((close) => speculative.has(genesisLearningOf(close, learnedNow())!.slot))) {
+          restore = true;    // a close on a slot still speculative: that value failed its close (section 3.0)
+        } else {
+          const state = learnedNow();
+          // applyAll: first write per slot per walk; returns the [slot, value] pairs it applied past the walk's
+          // first close, each distinctive (section 3.0), skipping any other later close.
+          const { later } = applyAll(read.closes);
+          for (const [slot, value] of later) speculative.set(slot, value);
+          if (later.length > 0) origin ??= { state, iteration };
+          continue;
+        }
+      } else if (read.passed) {
+        // A walk that passes with no closes accepts (:1314) once it compared every speculative value.
+        if (origin === undefined || confirms(speculative, passed)) {
+          origin = undefined;
+          accepted = true;
+          break;
+        }
+        restore = true;
+      } else if (origin !== undefined) {
+        restore = true;    // a stop the batches may have caused: learnDeclaration would throw on it (:1453, :1484)
+      }
+      if (!restore) {
+        // Today's rebinding (:1328-1331): the loop advances only through it. It runs only with no `origin`, so
+        // `speculative` is empty here.
+        ({ records: viewOuts, events: eventOuts, nodes: nodeOuts, sideCars: settledSideCars } =
+          learnDeclaration({ ..., reading: read.end }));
+      }
+    } catch (error) {
+      if (origin === undefined) throw error;
+      restore = true;
+    }
+  }
+  if (restore) {
+    ({ viewOuts, eventOuts, nodeOuts, settledSideCars } = origin!.state);
+    iteration = origin!.iteration - 1;
+    origin = undefined;
+    speculative.clear();
+    batching = false;
+    bumpFramedCounter('speculationRestores');
+  }
+}
+```
+
+- Today an iteration is one `evaluate` plus a recorded-close read. Here it is one walk, and the walk's `final` is the
+  acceptance verdict.
+- Exhaustion restores before the `!accepted` throw (`:1335`), so it and `constructorRevert` (`:1494`), which evaluates
+  the same program, run on the base's path. The twin's memo answers `constructorRevert` from the walk's verdict, so its
+  throw message is unchanged.
+- Throws happen only on a faithful walk with no `origin`, so the messages are today's.
+- `genesisLearningOf` matches only an `ok` `closeReading(close, readingBound)` (`:1452`).
