+## 5. Read-field rule (exact memo) and the structural recipe
+
+### 5.1 `framed/composer/run-memo.ts` (new): composer twin and memo
+
+```ts
+export const COMPOSER_MEMO: unique symbol = Symbol('composer run memo');
+/** The operands of the failed close an evaluation stopped on, attached to the state the twin returns. */
+export const FAILED_CLOSE: unique symbol = Symbol('failed close');
+
+/** How a faithful run ended, without any caller's plausibility bound. */
+export type RunStop =
+  | { readonly kind: 'passed' }
+  | { readonly kind: 'close'; readonly close: ReadDeclaration }
+  | { readonly kind: 'other'; readonly reading: DeclarationReading };
+export interface RunVerdict { readonly final: unknown; readonly passed: boolean; readonly stop?: RunStop }
+
+/** The fields a run read: `opcode * 0x10000 + index` (index 0 for transaction-wide reads). */
+export interface ReadNote { readonly keys: Set<number>; unbounded: boolean }
+/**
+ * Attached to every state the twin's `evaluate` returns: on a hit `{ keys: new Set(entry.fields.map(([key]) =>
+ * key)), unbounded: false }`, on a run its `ReadNote`, unbounded or not. The recipe's read roles come from it (5.2).
+ */
+export const RUN_READS: unique symbol = Symbol('run reads');
+
+/** A field snapshot: a copy up to 4 KiB (64 KiB for `own`), else the sha256 of the bytes. */
+export interface BytesSnapshot { readonly length: number; readonly bytes: Uint8Array }
+export type FieldAtom = BytesSnapshot | number | bigint | string | undefined;
+export type FieldValue = FieldAtom | readonly FieldAtom[];
+
+export function composerMachineOf<T extends object>(base: T): T;   // twin, or `base` when it has no origin
+export function composerMemoOf(vm: unknown): ComposerRunMemo | undefined;
+```
+
+**Twin.** `composerMachineOf(base)` behaves as follows:
+- It reads `base[PROVIDER_VM_ORIGIN]`. With no origin (a stock libauth VM, an observer VM, or a twin), it returns
+  `base`. Every provider's cached observerless VM has an origin, live ones included (SPEC F10).
+- Otherwise it returns a twin from `WeakMap<object, Twin>`, so there is one twin per base and the twin lives as long as
+  the provider's cached VM.
+
+The twin is built as follows:
+- `inner = createVirtualMachineBch2026ForProvider(origin.provider, observer, { standard: origin.standard,
+  recordCloseCopies: false })`. With an observer, this is a new, uncached VM. On a provider without the fast block
+  it is libauth's own instruction set and phase runner plus section 1.1's "Every provider" additions.
+- `twin = Object.create(inner)`, so `debug`, `verify`, `stateSuccess` and `boundedDebug` are inherited.
+- Overrides: `evaluate`, `boundedWalk`, and `[COMPOSER_MEMO]`.
+- The memo is disabled (the twin still counts) under `SOLIDC_DEBUG_FRAMED_LEGACY=1` (SPEC F7).
+
+**Observer.** It uses the `ProviderVmObserver` API at `createVirtualMachine.ts:867`, with no `operation` hook, so it is
+read-only and the stock operation runs. It sets `recordInactiveBranches: true`, so instruments Change B never installs
+branch skips on the twin (SPEC F10). `opcodes` are:
+- OP_CHECKSIG through OP_CHECKMULTISIGVERIFY (`0xac-0xaf`), the transaction signature checks;
+- OP_CHECKLOCKTIMEVERIFY and OP_CHECKSEQUENCEVERIFY (`0xb1`, `0xb2`);
+- OP_TXVERSION through OP_OUTPUTTOKENAMOUNT (`0xc2-0xd3`).
+
+OP_INPUTINDEX and OP_ACTIVEBYTECODE are constant for a given input and its own unlocking bytecode, which are part of
+the memo key. OP_CHECKDATASIG and OP_CHECKDATASIGVERIFY (`0xba`, `0xbb`) are not observed: they read only their stack
+operands (SPEC F11).
+
+```ts
+beforeOperation: (unknown) => {
+  const note = sink.note;
+  if (note === undefined || note.unbounded) return;
+  const state = unknown as { ip: number; instructions: readonly { opcode: number }[]; stack: Uint8Array[];
+    controlStack: readonly unknown[] };
+  if (state.controlStack.some((frame) => frame === false)) return;          // inactive branch (F7)
+  const opcode = state.instructions[state.ip]!.opcode;
+  if (opcode <= Op.OP_CHECKMULTISIGVERIFY) { note.unbounded = true; return; } // the signing serialization: all
+  if (opcode < Op.OP_UTXOVALUE) { note.keys.add(opcode * 0x10000); return; }  // CLTV, CSV, tx-wide fields
+  const top = state.stack[state.stack.length - 1];
+  const index = top === undefined ? undefined : vmNumberToBigInt(top);
+  if (typeof index !== 'bigint' || index < 0n || index > 0xffffn) { note.unbounded = true; return; }
+  note.keys.add(opcode * 0x10000 + Number(index));
+  // An index past the end fails with the count in its message (common/inspection.js:9,21,40): key the count too.
+  const { transaction } = (unknown as { program: { transaction: { inputs: unknown[]; outputs: unknown[] } } }).program;
+  const ofOutputs = opcode === Op.OP_OUTPUTVALUE || opcode === Op.OP_OUTPUTBYTECODE || opcode >= Op.OP_OUTPUTTOKENCATEGORY;
+  if (Number(index) >= (ofOutputs ? transaction.outputs : transaction.inputs).length) {
+    note.keys.add((ofOutputs ? Op.OP_TXOUTPUTCOUNT : Op.OP_TXINPUTCOUNT) * 0x10000);
+  }
+},
+```
+
+Twin `evaluate(program, options)`:
+1. `bumpFramedCounter('composerEvaluations')`.
+2. Without a `stateOverride`, if `memo.verdictFor(program)` is defined, bump `memoEvaluationHits` and return
+   `{ ...inner.stateClone(verdict.final), program, [FAILED_CLOSE]: closeOf(verdict) }`. The clone and the copied
+   close operands (`Uint8Array.from`, as `recordedClose` copies them) keep a caller that mutates the returned state
+   away from the stored verdict (SPEC F12).
+3. Otherwise:
+   - set `sink.note = { keys: new Set(), unbounded: false }`;
+   - run `inner.evaluate(program, options)` in a `try`/`finally` that clears `sink.note`;
+   - read `inner.lastStopClose()`;
+   - attach `[FAILED_CLOSE]` and `[RUN_READS]` to the returned state (a hit attaches both too);
+   - without a `stateOverride`, call `memo.note(program, note, { final: state, passed: inner.stateSuccess(state) ===
+     true, stop: stopOfEvaluation(state, close) })`;
+   - return the state.
+
+Twin `boundedWalk(program, options)`: set the sink, walk with `inner.boundedWalk`, clear the sink, and return
+`{ ...walk, reads: note }`. The reader notes the verdict (section 1.2, step 6). A suppressing walk is never noted.
+
+**Memo.**
+- Storage is `Map<number, Entry>` keyed by `program.inputIndex`, holding the latest entry only. An `Entry` is
+  `{ own, ownLock, fields: (readonly [key, FieldValue])[], verdict }`.
+- `note(...)`:
+  - When `unbounded`, delete the entry and bump `memoUnmemoizable`.
+  - Otherwise, snapshot:
+    - `own`: `inputs[i].unlockingBytecode`, copied when at most 64 KiB, else its sha256;
+    - `ownLock`: `sourceOutputs[i].lockingBytecode`, copied;
+    - each field: `fieldOf(program, key, i)`, copied when at most 4 KiB, else its sha256.
+  - Store `inner.stateClone(verdict.final)` with `program` deleted from the clone. It then neither keeps the 670 KB
+    program alive nor shares a container with the state the caller received (SPEC F12).
+  - Copy the stop's close operands (`Uint8Array.from`) whichever caller hands them in: a miss hands in the live stack
+    items (`network/createVirtualMachine.ts:547-553`). `readingOfStop` reads fresh copies. Other stack items stay
+    shared, as in libauth's own clone (`virtual-machine.js:41`).
+- `fieldOf` maps opcode to field:
+
+  | opcode | field |
+  |---|---|
+  | `0xc2` | `version` |
+  | `0xc3` | `inputs.length` |
+  | `0xc4` | `outputs.length` |
+  | `0xc5` | `locktime` |
+  | `0xc6` / `0xc7` | `sourceOutputs[i].valueSatoshis` / `.lockingBytecode` |
+  | `0xc8` / `0xc9` | `inputs[i].outpointTransactionHash` / `.outpointIndex` |
+  | `0xca` | `inputs[i].unlockingBytecode` |
+  | `0xcb` | `inputs[i].sequenceNumber` |
+  | `0xcc` / `0xcd` | `outputs[i].valueSatoshis` / `.lockingBytecode` |
+  | `0xce`-`0xd0` | `sourceOutputs[i].token`: `[category, nft?.capability]`, `nft?.commitment`, `amount` |
+  | `0xd1`-`0xd3` | the same fields of `outputs[i].token` |
+  | `0xb1` | `[locktime, inputs[own].sequenceNumber]` |
+  | `0xb2` | `[version, inputs[own].sequenceNumber]` |
+
+  An out-of-range index snapshots as `undefined`.
+- `verdictFor(program)` compares `own`, `ownLock` and every field: a tuple (`0xce`, `0xd1`, `0xb1`, `0xb2`) position by
+  position, a `BytesSnapshot` by length and then its copy or digest, anything else by `===`; values of different
+  shapes differ. On a mismatch it bumps `memoMisses`. With `SOLIDC_DEBUG_COMPOSER_MEMO_MISS=1` it logs the first
+  mismatching opcode and index.
+- `stopOfEvaluation(state, close)` answers only where the walk's reading is known exactly:
+  - success gives `{ kind: 'passed' }`;
+  - a recorder-attributed close gives `{ kind: 'close', close }`;
+  - a step error that is not at an EQUALVERIFY, with `ip - 1 >= 0` and its opcode defined and not `OP_BEGIN`, gives
+    `{ kind: 'other', reading: { ok: false, reason: 'not-a-close', opcode, error } }`. An `OP_UNTIL` back-jump
+    leaves `ip - 1` at the loop's `OP_BEGIN` (`bch-2026-loops.js:25`) where a walk names `OP_UNTIL`, so that case
+    returns `undefined`.
+  - Otherwise it returns `undefined`, and a reader then walks. That covers:
+    - phase errors (clean stack, control stack, P2SH match, malformed, length, push-only), matched against
+      `PHASE_ERRORS`: the twelve `AuthenticationErrorCommon` members both phase runners apply outside a step
+      (`network/createVirtualMachine.ts:184-306`; libauth `bch-2023-instruction-set.js:49-125`, inherited by 2026).
+      They are `requiresPushOnly`, `exceededMaximumBytecodeLength{Unlocking,Locking}`,
+      `malformed{Unlocking,Locking,P2sh}Bytecode`, `unmatchedP2shRedeemBytecode`,
+      `nonEmptyControlStack{Unlocking,Locking,Redeem}Bytecode` and `requiresCleanStack{Locking,Redeem}Bytecode`. An
+      error matches one when it equals it or continues it after a space (`format/error.js:34`);
+    - an EQUALVERIFY error with no recorder note (a limit error after a passing verify, or an empty stack);
+    - an error on the first step of an OP_INVOKE swap.
+  - A `RunVerdict` whose `stop` is undefined still answers evaluations, but never reads.
+
+**Lifetime and size.** One twin per base VM, so per provider. At most one entry per input index. Bytes are bounded
+by about 64 KiB per entry plus small fields.
+
+**Invariant.** Execution is a deterministic function of the program bytes it reads. Those are its own unlocking
+bytecode (the initial stack and the density budget), its own locking bytecode (P2SH), and the introspected fields, so
+every stack item is a function of them too. A transaction signature check also hashes the signing serialization,
+which covers fields the observer does not enumerate, so it makes the run unmemoizable. A data signature check reads
+only its stack operands and needs no key (SPEC F11). Equal bytes in all of these give an equal run, so a memo answer
+equals the run it replaces. The twin steps every instruction its base steps, so its run is the base's run.
+
+### 5.2 `framed/composer/recipe.ts` (new): the structural recipe
+
+**Key.** `compositionRecipeKey(plan: CompositionDraftPlan): string` is the sha256 of a canonical JSON with no byte
+values:
+- per master, in plan order:
+  - `code` = sha256 hex of `master.redeemScript` (memoized per array in a WeakMap; Q4 covers `artifact.fingerprint`);
+  - `entry` = `master.functionName`, the stop-site table's key, used only as an opaque key part;
+  - `args` = `argumentPushes.map((push) => push.length)`;
+  - `segments`: per entry, `(in === INDEX_NONE, out === INDEX_NONE, viewIn: 'carried' | 'stated',
+    viewOut: 'unstated' | 'carried' | 'stated')`;
+  - `calls`: `(kind, callee position, deferred)`;
+  - `callBaseBySite`;
+  - the counts of `events`, `sends` and `values`;
+  - `dispatches`;
+  - `enteredBy`/`origin` as positions;
+- minted masters: calls and segments shape;
+- the counts of `leading`, `userInputs`, `trailingOutputs` and `inputs`;
+- `tokenRuns`;
+- computed witnesses by master position;
+- whether `locktime`, `sequenceNumber` and `validator` are present.
+
+**Stored per master (no values).**
+
+```ts
+export interface StepRecipe {
+  /** The published site this fill stepped and the walks' learned counts, layer by layer. */
+  readonly site: number;
+  readonly layers: readonly number[];
+  /** The post-fill run stopped on a close the master could learn: a skip here would always look like a deviation. */
+  readonly afterLearnable: boolean;
+}
+export interface MasterRecipe {
+  readonly steps: readonly StepRecipe[];
+  readonly readKeys: readonly string[];
+  readonly readsAll: boolean;
+}
+export interface CompositionRecipe { readonly masters: readonly MasterRecipe[] }
+export const RECIPE_CAPACITY = 64;
+export function lookupRecipe(key: string): CompositionRecipe | undefined;  // refreshes recency; hits/misses
+export function storeRecipe(key: string, recipe: CompositionRecipe | undefined): void;  // evicts least recent
+export function dropRecipe(key: string): void;                             // recipeDeviations
+export function clearRecipes(): void;                                      // tests
+```
+
+- `readKeys` are opcode-and-role strings: `in:p<k>` (participant position), `in:u<k>`, `in:f<k>`, `out:p<k>`,
+  `out:t<k>`, `out:f<k>`, `in:own`, `tx`, and `in:x`/`out:x` for an index past the transaction. `observeAfter` maps
+  them from each run's `[RUN_READS]` (section 5.1) through the draft's layout (`indices`, `orderedIds`, `trailing`).
+- Uses of `readKeys`: a run that reads a role the recipe lacks is a deviation, and a `readsAll` master never skips.
+  Skips are never decided from `readKeys` alone, because a stale role set would skip a run whose read field changed.
+- Storage is a module-level `Map` used as an LRU (delete and re-set on a hit) with process lifetime. It holds only
+  structure.
+
+**Draft hooks.**
+- `ComposeDraftOptions` (`:503-512`) gains `recipe?: CompositionRecipe | 'record'`.
+- `createComposedDerivationHost` (`:1098-1115`) gains `recipe?: boolean`. When true and `composerMemoOf(vm)` is
+  defined, it computes the key and passes `lookupRecipe(key) ?? 'record'`. No recipe without the memo.
+- The draft keeps the following:
+  - per master: a fill ordinal, the recording of `StepRecipe`s, and the observed read roles;
+  - `recipeKey`, `recipeOff`, and the skip count.
+- `fill` (call sites only; read and segment-close sites never skip) follows these rules:
+  - `step = recipe?.masters[position]?.steps[ordinal]`.
+  - If `step.site !== site.site`, the sequence deviates: `dropRecipe`, set `recipeOff`, and continue normally.
+  - **Skip the learning walk** when `step.layers.length === 0`, `!step.afterLearnable`,
+    `!masterRecipe.readsAll`, and the memo cannot answer the read (`memo.verdictFor(programOf(...)) === undefined`).
+    Return `skippedLearning: true` and record the step as predicted.
+  - **Skip the confirming walk**: `skipsConfirmation(step, layers)` runs after each applying walk of the call (2.2)
+    and returns:
+    - `false` when `recipeOff` is set, or unless `step.layers.length === 1` and `layers.length === 1` (only right
+      after the call's first applying walk, on a single-layer recording);
+    - otherwise, when `layers[0] !== step.layers[0]`, a deviation: drop the key, set `recipeOff`, keep walking, and
+      return `false`;
+    - otherwise `true` exactly when `layers` is `[1]` and `!step.afterLearnable`. Then the walk applied one value, a
+      first close, so `provisional.size === 0`. A layer of more values leaves provisional ones, which only the
+      confirming walk settles (2.2), so it returns `false` without a deviation.
+
+    A skip returns `skippedLearning: true` and records the step as predicted.
+- `observeAfter(current, after)` alone records and checks read roles, after every post-fill run:
+  - It maps `after.reads` to roles; absent or unbounded reads are `'all'`.
+  - It always records: the master's role set takes the union, `'all'` sets `readsAll`, and `recipeRecording()` emits
+    the set sorted as `readKeys`.
+  - With the recipe on and the master not `readsAll`, `'all'` or a role outside `readKeys` is a role deviation.
+  - `afterLearnable` is whether `after.close` is defined and its operands match this master's `matchOf` (a placeholder
+    or a provisional value). The draft records it as the step's.
+  - A role deviation, or a learnable stop after a skip, calls `dropRecipe` (the one `recipeDeviations` bump) and sets
+    `recipeOff`.
+  - It returns `afterLearnable || roleDeviation`. The host replays only a skipped step.
+- `recipeRecording()` returns the recording, or `undefined` if any master's sequence ended early.
+
+**Host (`framed/composer/shipped-host.ts`).**
+- `ShippedMasterRun` (`:107-125`):
+  - `fill` returns `{ callee?, undo?, skippedLearning? }`;
+  - add `observeAfter?(block, after): boolean`.
+- `ExecutionStop` (`:127-150`): add `close?: { declared: Uint8Array; computed: Uint8Array }` and `reads?` (the
+  `BoundedWalk.reads` shape).
+- `runOnce` (`:215`): read `state[FAILED_CLOSE]` into `close` and `state[RUN_READS]` into `reads`, before its accepted
+  return (`:217`).
+- `step` (`:345-357`):
+
+```ts
+let filled = run.fill(site, block);
+let after = runOnce(vm, run.programFor(block));
+// A learning walk the recipe skipped is checked by the run that follows it: a stop on a close this master could
+// learn means the recipe was wrong, so the fill is undone and the step runs as it always did (the recipe is off now).
+if (run.observeAfter?.(block, after) === true && filled.skippedLearning === true) {
+  filled.undo?.();
+  filled = run.fill(site, block);
+  after = runOnce(vm, run.programFor(block));
+  run.observeAfter?.(block, after);   // the replayed run's roles and stop are recorded too
+}
+const { callee } = filled;
+// ... the repeated-site learnReached block (:348-356) as today ...
+lastStop.set(run.master, after);
+```
+
+`undo` restores `calleeRef`, the `visits` entry, the fill ordinal and the master's role set. The second `fill` runs
+`learnComputedValues`, because `recipeOff` is now set.
+
+### 5.3 Invariants: a stale recipe costs time, never correctness
+
+1. The recipe stores no values and no program bytes. Every learned value comes from a walk of the current program.
+2. The recipe never skips an evaluation, the final verdicts, the provider verifier, or a read or segment-close fill.
+   Only the exact memo skips evaluations.
+3. A skip happens only at a call-site fill on a composer twin. The post-fill run, which the host makes anyway, checks
+   it in the same step. A failed check undoes the fill and replays the step from the identical pre-fill state, so the
+   step's state and outcome are the normal path's. The cost is one wasted run.
+4. A derivation that skipped and then stalled is re-derived without the recipe, and that result stands
+   (section 3.1).
+5. No provisional value outlives the learning call that made it (section 2.2), and a confirming walk is skipped only
+   after a one-value layer, which leaves none. A skip therefore cannot carry an unconfirmed value into a signed
+   transaction.
+6. Every deviation drops the key. An expected value that was not learned, an unexpected learnable stop, a different
+   site sequence, or an unknown read role all count, and the draft records afresh.
+7. Residual: the check sees the post-fill run. A pre-fill learnable close that the post-fill run steps around would be
+   missed. That needs a body that branches on its own unfilled call record before the site. Two things guard it:
+   - the placeholder stays unlearned and is refused by `unlearnedViews()`/`requireLearnedViews`, or learned by a later
+     walk;
+   - `SOLIDC_DEBUG_FRAMED_RECIPE_VERIFY=1` runs every skipped walk anyway and throws on a misprediction, for the landing
+     check.
+
