+# Spec: probe instruments at every limit (sparse default, recorder for full traces, suppressing variants)
+
+> Component spec of [`../SPEC.md`](../SPEC.md), the one-goal implementation spec. Where this file and SPEC.md
+> section 4 disagree, SPEC.md wins, and SPEC.md section 4 answers this file's open questions. Written read-only
+> against `fcbd58a09`; "steps" and "the coordinator" refer to the planning that produced it.
+
+Worktree `/Code/cashscript/.worktrees/sdk-tx-perf` at `fcbd58a09`. Paths below are relative to
+`packages/solidcash/src` unless they start with `test/` (relative to `packages/solidcash`) or `docs/` (repo root).
+Scope follows the coordinator's re-approach: the default derivation probe is the sparse observer on every
+network; `forceFullDebug` and the full-trace callers use the faithful recorder; the full-debug env overrides keep
+libauth `debug()` reachable.
+
+## 0. Decisions
+
+1. Phase exits for limits-less (and non-fast) providers come from a new **phase-exit-only hook** that wraps the
+   `stateEvaluate` argument of libauth's own `instructionSet.evaluate` (Change A). Not `installCachedP2shEvaluator`:
+   the hook reports exactly the phases `debug()` records and changes nothing else (analysis in section 9).
+   Installed only when the observer passes `onPhaseComplete` and no cached P2SH evaluator was installed, so
+   consensus, preflight, mock-verifier and debug VMs (all observerless) are untouched.
+2. `installSparseProbeBranchSkips` moves out of the fast-path block (Change B) and is hardened for two script
+   shapes the static targets cannot express (a second `OP_ELSE`; an opcode libauth fails even when unexecuted).
+   Nothing else the observer path uses lives in that block (section 10).
+3. The sparse collector ignores states inside an inactive branch (Change F). Skipping becomes a pure speed-up and
+   the parity replay is exact.
+4. `evaluateProbeTrace`: overrides -> `debug()` (as today, reduced at <= 10k unless a route dump); `forceFullDebug`
+   -> recorder (reduced at <= 10k, whole above, as today); default -> sparse observer at every limit (Change D).
+5. `evaluateFaithfulOrDebugTrace` drops the `usesFastVmPaths` gate: recorder on every provider;
+   `SC_FORCE_FULL_PROBE_TRACE=1` selects `debug()` (Change E).
+6. Batch-collector API: exported `ProbeOperationWrapper`, a 4th parameter on `createFaithfulTraceVmForProvider`,
+   two separate per-provider caches (sparse and recorder) and `evaluateSuppressedProbeTrace` (Change H).
+7. Parity: `SOLIDC_DEBUG_TRACE_PARITY=1` compares recorder vs `debug()` state for state, and sparse vs a replay of
+   `debug()`'s executed probe states through a fresh collector; a test-only sink hands both traces to tests for
+   extractor-level and byte-level comparison on a live-like provider (Change G, section 12).
+8. Deploy derivation probes with the sparse observer at every limit (Change J).
+
+---
+
+## Change A - phase-exit-only hook (recorder VMs only)
+
+**File** `network/createVirtualMachine.ts`.
+
+**Current.** Phase exits exist only inside `installCachedP2shEvaluator` (`:155`, calls at `:227`, `:244`, `:293`),
+installed at `:927` inside `if (limits !== undefined && usesFastVmPaths(provider))` (`:923`). A provider without
+`consensusLimits` (every live network) or a non-simulator provider publishing <= 10k limits gets libauth's evaluate
+and no exits, so `createFaithfulTraceVmForProvider(..., onPhaseComplete)` silently records an incomplete trace.
+
+**New code.** Add next to `installCachedP2shEvaluator`:
+
+```ts
+/**
+ * Report each evaluation phase's exit state from libauth's own evaluator. `debug()` records a phase by passing its
+ * recorder as `stateEvaluate`, so wrapping that argument reports exactly the phases `debug()` records: none for a
+ * phase libauth refuses before evaluating (a malformed redeem script, a non-push unlocking script).
+ */
+function installPhaseExitHook(
+  instructionSet: ReturnType<typeof createInstructionSetBch2026>,
+  onPhaseComplete: (state: unknown) => void,
+): void {
+  const evaluate = instructionSet.evaluate;
+  instructionSet.evaluate = (program, options) => evaluate(program, {
+    ...options,
+    stateEvaluate: (state) => {
+      const exit = options.stateEvaluate(state);
+      onPhaseComplete(exit);
+      return exit;
+    },
+  });
+}
+```
+
+Install it in `buildVirtualMachineBch2026ForProvider` right after the fast-path block closes (`:1099`), before
+`type State` (`:1100`):
+
+```ts
+  if (runPhases === undefined && observer?.onPhaseComplete !== undefined) {
+    installPhaseExitHook(instructionSet, observer.onPhaseComplete);
+  }
+```
+
+(`createVirtualMachine` reads `instructionSet.evaluate` at call time, `virtual-machine.js` `evaluate`/`debug`, so
+position before `:1149` is enough; keep it next to the other installs for reading order.)
+
+**Invariants.**
+- Installed iff an observer carries `onPhaseComplete` and the cached P2SH evaluator is absent. Today only
+  `createFaithfulTraceVmForProvider` callers pass it: `cachedFaithfulTraceVm` (`faithful-probe-trace.ts:147`) and
+  `evaluateBoundedProbeCandidates` (`:97`). Observerless VMs (`createPreparedTxVerifier.ts:65-67`,
+  `cachedDebugVm`, `observerlessVmByProvider`) and every other observer are unchanged.
+- The fast path keeps its own exits (`:227/:244/:293`); the two never stack.
+- Exit timing equals the cached evaluator's: right after each `stateEvaluate`, before libauth's error,
+  control-stack and clean-stack checks.
+
+**Failure behaviour.** An exception from `onPhaseComplete` propagates out of `evaluate` (as on the fast path). The
+recorder's callback only snapshots.
+
+---
+
+## Change B - branch skips on every sparse observer VM, hardened
+
+**File** `network/createVirtualMachine.ts`.
+
+**Current.** `:1096-1098` installs `installSparseProbeBranchSkips` (`:699`) only inside the fast block. A
+limits-less observer VM steps through inactive branches and calls `beforeOperation` for inactive instructions
+(the observer wrapper at `:1128-1133` sits outside libauth's `conditionallyEvaluate`).
+
+**New code.** Move the three lines after the block's closing brace (`:1099`), unchanged in condition:
+
+```ts
+  }
+  // Every sparse observer skips inactive branches at every limit: the skip reads static branch targets and charges
+  // each skipped instruction's base cost, so stop states and metrics match stepping.
+  if (observer !== undefined && observer.recordInactiveBranches !== true) {
+    installSparseProbeBranchSkips(instructionSet);
+  }
+```
+
+Order on the fast path is unchanged (diagnostic wraps -> skips -> commitment overrides `:1101` -> observer `:1117`
+-> step trace `:1148`).
+
+Harden `targetsFor` (`:704-725`) for the BCH-2026 instruction set the VM builds. Static targets are wrong for three
+shapes a compiler never emits but inline assembly can (corrected during commit 1; an earlier draft listed
+`OP_VERIF`, `OP_VERNOTIF`, `OP_2MUL` and `OP_2DIV`, which fail unexecuted only in the 2023 set: in 2026 those bytes
+are `OP_BEGIN`, `OP_UNTIL`, `OP_LSHIFTNUM` and `OP_RSHIFTNUM`, and no opcode fails unexecuted):
+- a second `OP_ELSE`, which toggles the branch again;
+- a loop that crosses a conditional's boundary. An inactive `OP_BEGIN` pushes a loop marker and an inactive
+  `OP_UNTIL` pops one (`bch-2026-loops.js`), and `OP_ELSE`/`OP_ENDIF` fail on a marker (`flow-control.js:36-52`), so
+  every conditional around the crossing steps;
+- a region that would pass the control-stack limit. Inactive `OP_IF`/`OP_NOTIF`/`OP_BEGIN` still push, and libauth's
+  `every` fails above `maximumControlStackDepth` (100, `bch-2025-instruction-set.js:51`). Each target carries the
+  region's deepest relative nesting, and `jumpTo` steps when `controlStack.length + depth` would pass the limit.
+
+A stepped conditional keeps `-1` targets, so `jumpTo` (`target <= state.ip`) steps it exactly as libauth. The scan
+keeps one stack of open conditionals and loops; a closed frame hands its peak depth to its parent.
+
+**Why the skip is exact (from the code).** Inactive operations are `conditionallyEvaluate` no-ops; the VM's
+`afterOperation` still counts each one, which `jumpTo` reproduces (`evaluatedInstructionCount += target - ip - 1`);
+libauth's `every` (2025 `:31-58`, 2026 `:46-55`) derives `operationCost` from that count, so the cost after the jump
+equals the stepped cost. Push-size checks also run unexecuted (`push.js:105`) but no push can exceed the stack-item
+limit inside a script bounded by the same limit (10,000 standard; equal values on the mock profiles). The legacy
+top-level `operationCount` is under-counted for skipped non-push opcodes (2023 `incrementOperationCount` wraps the
+conditional op, `:282`); nothing enforces it after 2025 and no consumer reads it. A budget crossed inside a skipped
+region errors at the `OP_IF`/`OP_ELSE` instead of the k-th inactive instruction: same error type, different `ip`.
+
+**Who gets skips newly (non-fast providers only).** `cachedProbeVm` (now the default instrument), the deploy observer
+(Change J), and the ungated message-bus observers: `message-bus/preflight.ts:346`, `:3077`,
+`computed-value-chunks.ts:271`, `:512`, `computed-dynamic-chunks.ts:208`, `stb-repair-computed-chunk-output.ts:261`
+(all already drop inactive states themselves), `deferred-compute-early-revert.ts:67` (does not: inactive reads stop
+setting `readUnresolvedValue`, matching what the mock suites already exercise), and debug-only observers
+(`preflight.ts:1127`, `:1278`, `:1913`, `:2187`, `:2208`, `:2265`, `:2334`). `stb-covenant-failure-trace.ts:69` stays
+relaxed-gated. Faithful recorders (`recordInactiveBranches: true`, `:858`) never skip.
+
+**Failure behaviour.** None new; a script the hardening marks stepped runs at stock speed.
+
+---
+
+## Change C - probe-only operation wrapper API
+
+**File** `network/createVirtualMachine.ts`.
+
+**Current.** `ProviderVmObserver` (`:782`) is unexported; its `operation` hook (`:786-788`) is dispatched at
+`:1130-1132` (read at call time) but `createFaithfulTraceVmForProvider` (`:850`) cannot pass one.
+
+**New code.**
+
+```ts
+/** A probe-only wrapper around one observed operation; it returns `operation(state)` for anything it keeps. */
+export type ProbeOperationWrapper = (
+  opcode: number, state: unknown, operation: (state: never) => unknown,
+) => unknown;
+
+export type ProviderVmObserver = {
+  ...                       // unchanged fields
+  operation?: ProbeOperationWrapper;
+  ...
+};
+
+export function createFaithfulTraceVmForProvider(...);   // unchanged: with C1 no recorder suppresses
+```
+
+**Invariants.** The wrapper sees every observed opcode (all 256 for the recorder, `PROBE_TRACE_OPCODES` for the
+sparse VM, which includes `OP_EQUALVERIFY`). `beforeOperation` runs before the wrapper, so the trace keeps the
+failing check's operands. On the fast path the wrapped `operation` already includes the failed-close recorder
+(`:519`) and diagnostic wraps; on live it is libauth's op. `applyError` returns a shallow copy
+(`common/errors.js:97`), so a suppressing wrapper returns `{ ...next }` without the `error` key: a failed
+`OP_EQUALVERIFY` has already consumed both operands and the boolean (`opEqual` then `opVerify`), the same stack a
+pass leaves.
+
