+## Change H - suppressing variants for the batch collector
+
+**File** `stateful/faithful-probe-trace.ts` (caches `:50-67`, `cachedFaithfulTraceVm` `:147-185`,
+`evaluateFaithfulProbeTrace` `:194-206`, `cachedProbeVm` `:556-692`).
+
+**Refactor (no behaviour change for faithful callers).**
+- `cachedFaithfulTraceVm` -> `installFaithfulTraceVm(provider, cached, operation?)` that builds `cached.vm` with
+  callbacks closing over `cached` (they read `cached.trace` at call time, which `runFaithfulTrace` swaps), passing
+  `operation` as the 4th argument of `createFaithfulTraceVmForProvider`; the faithful cache calls it without one.
+- `evaluateFaithfulProbeTrace` body -> `runFaithfulTrace(cached, program)` (reset, evaluate, push the final snapshot,
+  swap the array); `evaluateFaithfulProbeTrace` = `runFaithfulTrace(cachedFaithfulTraceVm(provider), program)`.
+- `cachedProbeVm` body -> `installProbeVm(provider, cached, operation?)` (sets `cached.collector` and `cached.vm`; the
+  observer gets `...(operation === undefined ? {} : { operation })`).
+
+**New code.**
+
+```ts
+interface SuppressingSlot { operation: ProbeOperationWrapper | undefined }
+const suppressingProbeVmCache = new WeakMap<NetworkProvider, CachedProbeVm & SuppressingSlot>();
+const suppressingTraceVmCache = new WeakMap<NetworkProvider, CachedFaithfulTraceVm & SuppressingSlot>();
+
+/** Run the wrapper the current evaluation installed, or the operation unchanged. */
+function slotDispatcher(slot: SuppressingSlot): ProbeOperationWrapper {
+  return (opcode, state, operation) => (slot.operation === undefined
+    ? operation(state as never) : slot.operation(opcode, state, operation));
+}
+
+function cachedSuppressingProbeVm(provider: NetworkProvider): CachedProbeVm & SuppressingSlot {
+  const existing = suppressingProbeVmCache.get(provider);
+  if (existing !== undefined) return existing;
+  const cached = { operation: undefined } as CachedProbeVm & SuppressingSlot;
+  installProbeVm(provider, cached, slotDispatcher(cached));
+  suppressingProbeVmCache.set(provider, cached);
+  return cached;
+}
+// cachedSuppressingTraceVm: same shape over installFaithfulTraceVm with { trace: [], phaseExits: 0 }.
+
+/**
+ * Evaluate a probe on the batch collector's own VMs, `operation` wrapping every observed operation for this
+ * evaluation only; the faithful caches never carry a wrapper. Returns undefined while a full-debug override selects
+ * libauth's `debug()`, which has no operation hook: the caller then probes cleanly. Not reentrant: a nested call
+ * throws before it touches the slot or the collector (SPEC C4).
+ */
+export function evaluateSuppressedProbeTrace(
+  provider: NetworkProvider,
+  program: ProbeProgram,
+  operation: ProbeOperationWrapper,
+  forceFullDebug = false,
+): AuthenticationProgramStateCommon[] | undefined {
+  const debugEnv = ...;
+  if (debugEnv?.SC_FORCE_FULL_PROBE_TRACE === '1' || debugEnv?.SOLIDC_DEBUG_ROUTE_CONCISE === '1'
+    || debugEnv?.SOLIDC_DEBUG_ROUTE_FULL_OPS === '1') return undefined;
+  if (forceFullDebug) {
+    const cached = cachedSuppressingTraceVm(provider);
+    cached.operation = operation;
+    try {
+      const trace = runFaithfulTrace(cached, program);
+      return (provider.consensusLimits?.maximumInputBytes ?? 10_000) <= 10_000 ? reduceProbeTrace(trace) : trace;
+    } finally {
+      cached.operation = undefined;
+    }
+  }
+  const cached = cachedSuppressingProbeVm(provider);
+  if (cached.operation !== undefined) {
+    throw new Error('evaluateSuppressedProbeTrace: nested evaluation on the collector VM');
+  }
+  cached.operation = operation;
+  try {
+    cached.collector.reset();
+    return cached.collector.finish(cached.vm.evaluate(program) as AuthenticationProgramStateCommon);
+  } finally {
+    cached.operation = undefined;
+  }
+}
+```
+
+**Invariants.** Separate VM instances per provider (two extra VMs per provider, built lazily). Only the two
+`cachedSuppressing*` functions pass a dispatcher; with an empty slot it is a pass-through, so a stray evaluation on
+those VMs is faithful. The wrapper is set for one synchronous evaluation and cleared in `finally`, including when it
+throws. A nested call throws instead of replacing the outer wrapper or resetting the outer trace (SPEC C4). Same
+output shape as `evaluateProbeTrace` in the matching mode. No parity, no dumps.
+
+**Failure behaviour.** Wrapper exceptions propagate (slot cleared). `undefined` under overrides.
