+# Collector integration spec: loops, ownership, provisional mark
+
+> Component spec of [`../SPEC.md`](../SPEC.md), the one-goal implementation spec. Where this file and SPEC.md
+> section 4 disagree, SPEC.md wins, and SPEC.md section 4 answers this file's open questions. Written read-only
+> against `fcbd58a09`; "steps" and "the coordinator" refer to the planning that produced it.
+
+Worktree `/Code/cashscript/.worktrees/sdk-tx-perf`, branch `perf/sdk-tx-perf` at `fcbd58a09`. Paths are relative
+to `packages/solidcash/src` unless stated. Line numbers are at `fcbd58a09`. Commit 1 moved three of the cited files:
+every cited line of `stateful/StatefulContract.ts` is 216 lower at HEAD; in `stateful/sc-derive-deploy-commitments.ts`
+lines 340-707 are 3 lower and later lines 1 lower; in `stateful/sc-derive-full-phase2-iteration-probe.ts` lines after
+155 are 1 higher; in `stateful/stb-measure-and-fund-covenant-fee.ts` lines after 33 are 5 higher. No other cited file
+changed. Design: `docs/wip/sdk-tx-perf/DESIGN.md` sections 2, 6, 7.
+Removed prior art: `8d335f51f` (relaxed discovery, gated
+`!hasRuntimeLoopTransfers && (stateCount > 1 || (stateCount === 0 && mappingEntryCount > 1))`, counted a suppressing
+run as `faithfulProbeHadError`, passed `firstWriteWins = outputVerificationMismatchObserved` at the two phase-2
+state/entry sites, ran the cleaned rescan relaxed unconditionally).
+
+## 0. Decisions
+
+1. **A suppressing run never ends a loop.** Every exit rule (pass, fixed point, stable key, oscillation throw,
+   "no progress" break, convergence) is evaluated only on a run that suppressed nothing. Every run counts against
+   the loop's own bound, and the run that would reach it is admitted with `lastRun` and runs clean (SPEC L1).
+   Consequence: every loop's last evaluation is clean, so the "clean exit probe" of DESIGN 7.4 is structural (no
+   separate post-loop probe). The cap exit is reached only after a clean run.
+2. **One shared loop helper** (`stateful/collector-loop.ts`) owns: mode admission by transaction fingerprint
+   (mode-aware fixed point, "learned nothing", candidate cycle), the clean last run, the temporary
+   `SOLIDC_FAITHFUL_DERIVATION` development oracle (SPEC B2), the run record, the faithful trace for stack-scan
+   readers and the first-write boundary for extractors. Four loops use it; the final repair has its own (section 9).
+3. **"Learned nothing" and "cycle" are detected by the next candidate's fingerprint**: after a suppressing run, any
+   repeated candidate (same as the last, or already evaluated in either mode) turns suppression off for the rest of
+   the loop and is evaluated clean. This is the "reset the fixed-point fingerprint" rule; no mode string is mixed
+   into the fingerprint.
+4. **Clean runs use today's instrument** (`evaluateProbeTrace(provider, program, forceFullDebug)`); only `mode ===
+   'suppress'` calls `evaluateCollectorProbe`. With `SOLIDC_FAITHFUL_DERIVATION=1` every loop runs today's code path.
+   It is a development oracle, removed at the end of the goal, and no committed test uses it (SPEC B2, B4).
+5. **Ownership is type-based on the probe itself**: a non-minting NFT of a category this builder settles, not an
+   object the caller added through `addOutput()`, not an SCID identity commitment. The STB coordinate accessors are
+   model coordinates and drift from the materialized probe (dummy insertion, compose block bases, pads/chunks spliced
+   by materializers); the type rule cannot drift and covers every family they describe (section 3).
+6. **The provisional mark is scoped by the evaluated input** (`'root'` or `group:<i>`): a clean run of input A does
+   not validate values B's covenant computed. API keeps the coordinator's names with a scope argument.
+7. **First write wins past the faithful prefix** (SPEC L3). Every phase-2, cleaned-rescan, phase-1 and deploy
+   extraction site that today passes `false` passes `firstWriteFrom(run)`: `false` for a clean run, else the
+   faithful prefix length, `firstSuppressedTraceIndex + 1`. Observations in the prefix keep today's last-write rule,
+   so a suppressing run learns at every output what a clean run of the same transaction learns, with the same value;
+   past the prefix an output already learned keeps its value (section 5.4). Sites already passing `true` stay.
+8. **Stack-scan readers read the faithful trace** of a suppressing run: the trace a clean run of the same transaction
+   returns, which the collector keeps at the first suppression (`faithfulTrace`, collector-probe section 3). It holds
+   the observations through the suppressed check, the full stacks of the 96 before it, the evidence state and the
+   failed terminal state. A slice of the run's own trace has none of the last three: its window and evidence move
+   on. Readers: `dynamic-chunks:160,:184`, `value-chunks:97`, `runtime-loop:70`, the deferred keccak and ecrecover
+   resolvers (`StatefulContract.ts:5943-5944`), the graph-event readers and the event fallback (`apply-events.ts:188-191`,
+   `:200`), phase-1 `deriveRouteValueChunks`, deploy `observeValueChunkRuns` and its keccak read, and the repair's
+   EQUALVERIFY (geometry) branch. They assume the trace ends at the first failure. Past it they can pick up
+   placeholder-derived stack items and change geometry, and a learned keccak preimage is never re-learned
+   (`StatefulTransactionBuilder.ts:3674`).
+9. **An exception after a suppressing run is a fallback, not a failure**, while the loop's bound allows another run:
+   suppression turns off and the loop continues from the current builder state (section 5.6). Otherwise, and after a
+   clean run, the exception propagates unchanged.
+10. **Speculative chunk growth reconnected**: `outputVerificationMismatchObserved: suppressed`.
+11. **Final repair** suppresses inside its own observer VM (needs hooks, section 1), keeps first claim per output
+    after the first suppression, releases (does not record) suppressed claims in the cycle history, and its exits are
+    already faithful (it returns only after a passing `assertFinalizedTransactionCovenants`). It does not touch the STB
+    mark.
+12. **Compose needs no code change**: every composed participant is built through `StatefulFunctionCall.build()`
+    -> `buildFinalized`, which asserts (section 4.3).
+
+## 1. The collector primitive this part consumes
+
+The shapes are `spec/collector-probe.md` section 3, binding (SPEC C2); module `./collector-probe.js`.
+
+- `evaluateCollectorProbe(provider, program, session): CollectorProbeResult | undefined`. `undefined` means a
+  full-debug override is set, and the caller evaluates as a clean run (section 2).
+- `firstSuppressedTraceIndex` is the suppressed check's index in `trace`, -1 when nothing was suppressed. The faithful
+  prefix is `trace.slice(0, firstSuppressedTraceIndex + 1)`: the observations a clean run of the same transaction
+  records, without its evidence and terminal states. Extractors use it as the first-write boundary (decision 7).
+- `faithfulTrace` is the whole trace that clean run returns, kept at the first suppression (decision 8).
+- `createCollectorHooks(session)` serves the two loops that own their observer VM: the deploy loop, whose
+  `observeValueChunkRuns` reads `stack[-6..-3]` at `OP_OUTPUTBYTECODE`, wider than the sparse projection, and the final
+  repair, which observes live (`stb-repair-computed-chunk-output.ts:261`). The caller merges `hooks.opcodes` into its
+  observer set, calls `hooks.beforeOperation(state, recorded)` with its own recorded flag (sections 8 and 9.1),
+  installs `hooks.operation`, and reads the live `hooks.suppressedCount` and `hooks.firstFailure`.
+- `session.ownsValueOutput` owns value pins (section 3.3).
+
+## 2. New module `stateful/collector-loop.ts`
+
+```ts
+/**
+ * Loop-side collector rules (DESIGN 7.4, SPEC L1): suppression is on by default, a suppressing run never ends a loop,
+ * the last run a loop's bound allows is clean, and a repeated candidate switches suppression off for the loop.
+ */
+import type { AuthenticationProgramStateCommon } from '@bitauth/libauth/build/lib/vm/vm-types.js';
+import type { CollectionInfo, EntryAccessAbi } from '@solidcash/utils';
+import type NetworkProvider from '../network/NetworkProvider.js';
+import type { createVirtualMachineBch2026ForProvider } from '../network/createVirtualMachine.js';
+import { evaluateCollectorProbe, type CollectorSession } from './collector-probe.js';
+import { evaluateProbeTrace } from './faithful-probe-trace.js';
+
+export type CollectorMode = 'suppress' | 'clean';
+export type CollectorScope = 'root' | `group:${number}`;
+export type FinalizationSite = 'build' | 'send';
+type ProbeProgram = Parameters<ReturnType<typeof createVirtualMachineBch2026ForProvider>['evaluate']>[0];
+
+export type CollectorLoopName = 'phase2' | 'cleaned-rescan' | 'phase1-entries' | 'deploy';
+
+export interface CollectorRun {
+  readonly trace: AuthenticationProgramStateCommon[];
+  /** Suppressed comparisons; 0 makes the run the faithful verdict. */
+  readonly suppressedCount: number;
+  /** `firstSuppressedTraceIndex + 1` for a suppressing run, else `trace.length`. */
+  readonly faithfulPrefixLength: number;
+  /** The trace a clean run of the same transaction returns (decision 8); `trace` for a clean run. */
+  readonly faithfulTrace: AuthenticationProgramStateCommon[];
+}
+
+/** A run the loop did not evaluate itself but records as clean (the phase-1 trace seed, section 7). */
+export function cleanCollectorRun(trace: AuthenticationProgramStateCommon[]): CollectorRun {
+  return { trace, suppressedCount: 0, faithfulPrefixLength: trace.length, faithfulTrace: trace };
+}
+
+/** Oracle switch: every collector loop runs today's faithful path. Final bytes must not change. */
+export function collectorDisabledByEnvironment(): boolean {
+  return (globalThis as { process?: { env?: Record<string, string | undefined> } })
+    .process?.env?.SOLIDC_FAITHFUL_DERIVATION === '1';
+}
+
+/** Stack-scan readers see what a clean run of the same transaction would show them (decision 8). */
+export function faithfulScanTrace(run: CollectorRun): AuthenticationProgramStateCommon[] {
+  return run.faithfulTrace;
+}
+
+/** The extractors' `firstWriteWins` for this run (decision 7): `false` for a clean run, else the prefix end. */
+export function firstWriteFrom(run: Pick<CollectorRun, 'suppressedCount' | 'faithfulPrefixLength'>): false | number {
+  return run.suppressedCount === 0 ? false : run.faithfulPrefixLength;
+}
+
+export function evaluateCollectorRun(
+  provider: NetworkProvider, program: ProbeProgram, mode: CollectorMode, session: CollectorSession,
+): CollectorRun {
+  if (mode === 'clean') return cleanCollectorRun(evaluateProbeTrace(provider, program));
+  const result = evaluateCollectorProbe(provider, program, session);
+  // Undefined under the full-debug overrides: probe cleanly (SPEC I6).
+  if (result === undefined) return cleanCollectorRun(evaluateProbeTrace(provider, program));
+  if (result.suppressedCount === 0) return cleanCollectorRun(result.trace);
+  return {
+    trace: result.trace,
+    suppressedCount: result.suppressedCount,
+    faithfulPrefixLength: result.firstSuppressedTraceIndex + 1,
+    // Set whenever something was suppressed (collector-probe section 3).
+    faithfulTrace: result.faithfulTrace!,
+  };
+}
+
+export interface CollectorLoop {
+  readonly suppressing: boolean;
+  readonly lastRunSuppressed: boolean;
+  /**
+   * Mode for `candidate`, or 'fixed-point' when a clean run already gave this candidate's verdict. `lastRun`: the
+   * loop's bound allows no run after this one, so it runs clean (SPEC L1).
+   */
+  admit(candidate: string, fixedPoint: 'previous' | 'seen', lastRun?: boolean): CollectorMode | 'fixed-point';
+  /** Mode for a loop without a fixed-point exit (deploy, cleaned rescan). */
+  mode(candidate: string, lastRun?: boolean): CollectorMode;
+  record(run: CollectorRun): void;
+  stopSuppressing(): void;
+}
+
+export function createCollectorLoop(options: {
+  eligible: boolean; loop: CollectorLoopName; scope?: CollectorScope;
+}): CollectorLoop {
+  let suppressing = options.eligible && !collectorDisabledByEnvironment();
+  let lastRunSuppressed = false;
+  let lastCandidate: string | undefined;
+  let pending: string | undefined;
+  const clean = new Set<string>();
+  const suppressed = new Set<string>();
+  const stop = (): void => { suppressing = false; };
+  const admit = (
+    candidate: string, fixedPoint: 'previous' | 'seen' | 'never', lastRun = false,
+  ): CollectorMode | 'fixed-point' => {
+    pending = candidate;
+    const repeated = candidate === lastCandidate || clean.has(candidate) || suppressed.has(candidate);
+    // A suppressing run that changed nothing, or a candidate cycle: finish this loop faithfully.
+    if (lastRunSuppressed && repeated) {
+      stop();
+      return 'clean';
+    }
+    if ((fixedPoint === 'previous' && candidate === lastCandidate)
+      || (fixedPoint === 'seen' && clean.has(candidate))) return 'fixed-point';
+    if (suppressing && suppressed.has(candidate)) stop();
+    // The last run a loop's bound allows is clean; a bound that grows later may suppress again.
+    return suppressing && !lastRun ? 'suppress' : 'clean';
+  };
+  return {
+    get suppressing(): boolean { return suppressing; },
+    get lastRunSuppressed(): boolean { return lastRunSuppressed; },
+    admit: (candidate, fixedPoint, lastRun) => admit(candidate, fixedPoint, lastRun),
+    mode: (candidate, lastRun) => admit(candidate, 'never', lastRun) as CollectorMode,
+    record(run: CollectorRun): void {
+      lastRunSuppressed = run.suppressedCount > 0;
+      if (pending !== undefined) (lastRunSuppressed ? suppressed : clean).add(pending);
+      lastCandidate = pending;
+      pending = undefined;
+      if ((globalThis as { process?: { env?: Record<string, string | undefined> } })
+        .process?.env?.SOLIDC_DEBUG_COLLECTOR === '1') {
+        console.error('collector-run', JSON.stringify({
+          loop: options.loop, scope: options.scope, suppressed: run.suppressedCount, states: run.trace.length,
+          prefix: run.faithfulPrefixLength,
+        }));
+      }
+    },
+    stopSuppressing: stop,
+  };
+}
+```
+(`mode()` never yields 'fixed-point' because `'never'` disables that branch; implement with an internal
+overload instead of the cast if lint objects.)
+
+```ts
+/** Provisional carve-outs (DESIGN 2.2): single-NFT layouts and array collections stay faithful until lifted. */
+export function collectorLayoutEligible(
+  stateCount: number,
+  entryAccesses: readonly Pick<EntryAccessAbi, 'collection'>[] | undefined,
+  collections: readonly Pick<CollectionInfo, 'name' | 'kind'>[] | undefined,
+): boolean {
+  if (stateCount === 1) return false;
+  return !(entryAccesses ?? []).some((access) => (collections ?? []).some((collection) => (
+    collection.name === access.collection && collection.kind === 'array'
+  )));
+}
+
+/** Derivation-scoped record of collector scopes whose latest run suppressed a comparison (DESIGN 7.4). */
+export class ProvisionalMark {
+  private readonly scopes = new Set<CollectorScope>();
+  private readonly runs = new Map<CollectorScope, { suppressed: number; clean: number }>();
+
+  record(scope: CollectorScope, run: Pick<CollectorRun, 'suppressedCount'>): void {
+    const counts = this.runs.get(scope) ?? { suppressed: 0, clean: 0 };
+    if (run.suppressedCount > 0) {
+      this.scopes.add(scope);
+      counts.suppressed += 1;
+    } else {
+      this.scopes.delete(scope);
+      counts.clean += 1;
+    }
+    this.runs.set(scope, counts);
+  }
+
+  get provisional(): boolean { return this.scopes.size > 0; }
+
+  counts(): ReadonlyMap<CollectorScope, Readonly<{ suppressed: number; clean: number }>> { return this.runs; }
+
+  assertClear(site: FinalizationSite): void {
+    if (this.scopes.size === 0) return;
+    throw new Error(`Stateful ${site} refused: the latest probe of ${[...this.scopes].join(', ')} suppressed a `
+      + 'failed check and no faithful run verified it.');
+  }
+}
+
+/** Record one collector run's verdict on the builder's mark. */
+export function recordCollectorVerdict(
+  stb: { markProvisional(scope: CollectorScope): void; clearProvisional(scope: CollectorScope): void },
+  scope: CollectorScope, run: Pick<CollectorRun, 'suppressedCount'>,
+): void {
+  if (run.suppressedCount > 0) stb.markProvisional(scope);
+  else stb.clearProvisional(scope);
+}
+
+/** Complete fingerprint of an evaluated program: transaction plus spent outputs (as the phase-2 fixed point). */
+export function fingerprintProbeProgram(
+  program: Pick<ProbeProgram, 'transaction' | 'sourceOutputs'>, lockCache: WeakMap<Uint8Array, string>,
+): string;
+```
+`fingerprintProbeProgram` is lines `sc-derive-full-phase2-iteration-probe.ts:96-112` moved verbatim (it returns the
+same string, so phase 2 is unchanged); `lockCache` holds `hash256(lock)` hex like
+`sc-prepare-derive-full-phase2-loop.ts` `fingerprintLockingBytecode`. Phase 2 keeps passing its existing cache.
+
+Diagnostic (section 13): under `SOLIDC_DEBUG_COLLECTOR=1`, `record()` prints one `collector-run` line per
+evaluation with `loop`, `scope`, `suppressed`, `states` and `prefix`; the final repair prints its own (section 9.2).
+Test 17 reads these lines, so their fields are part of this spec.
+
+Invariants: a run with `suppressedCount === 0` is a faithful verdict whatever the mode; `record()` is called exactly
+once per evaluation, plus once for the phase-1 trace seed (section 7); `admit/mode` exactly once before it; a run
+admitted with `lastRun` is clean. Each loop passes `lastRun` from its own bound (sections 5-9), and every run,
+suppressing or clean, counts against that bound.
