+loops and across re-derivations of the same STB); by decision 1 every loop ends with a clean run of its scope, so a
+completed derivation leaves it empty. It can stay set only when an exception escapes after a suppressing run whose
+fallback could not run (section 5.6). That exception reaches the caller, and finalizing the same builder without a new
+derivation refuses.
