+### 5.5 Nested probes stay faithful (`sc-apply-derive-full-nested-*.ts`)
+
+`sc-apply-derive-full-nested-value-chunk-pins.ts:166` keeps `evaluateProbeTrace` (+ `compactFaithfulProbeTrace`),
+never the collector, because:
+1. Their extractors read the **terminal failing frame** (`extractFailingValueChunkCommitments`, the retained
+   terminal identity-count equality, `isValueChunkIdentityCountPin`); a suppressing run moves the terminal state to
+   the end of the program and destroys that observation.
+2. `nestedProbeHadError` gates the phase-2 pass exit and `needsPassingProbe`; a suppressing nested run would need its
+   own clean confirmation per call group per iteration, cancelling the gain.
+3. They run once per root iteration on the same `transaction2`; the root collector already cuts root iterations to
+   `d + 1`, which cuts nested probes proportionally.
+4. They are one-shot evaluations inside another loop's iteration and own no clean exit; suppression is allowed only
+   in a loop that does.
