+## 11. Lifting the carve-outs (`stateCount == 1`, `kind === 'array'`)
+
+Why they should be safe now: the old clobbering came from relaxing the next `OP_EQUALVERIFY` after any observed
+introspection; in the sparse trace an unrelated equality (a slice or element comparison) paired with the pending
+`OP_OUTPUTTOKENCOMMITMENT` and was read as the state commitment. Now (a) the collector suppresses only a comparison
+with one operand equal to the output's current commitment at an owned output, (b) the extractor skips equalities that
+do not name that value (`trace-commitment-helpers.ts:165-169`), and (c) first write wins. A later placeholder-derived
+pin for the same output is ignored; a garbage first pin is a dependent layer and is re-learned by the next run.
+
+Procedure: land with `collectorLayoutEligible` in place; then delete its body (return `true`) and run the two
+carve-out tests below once. If both pass, delete the function and its call sites (phase 2, cleaned rescan, phase 1,
+deploy); if one fails, keep that carve-out and report it. The tests must prove they exercise the carve-out:
+
+- `test/e2e/CollectorCarveOuts.test.ts`, case "single-NFT layout with a fixed array": source
