+New code:
+
+```ts
+/**
+ * Whether the console.log printer below can print anything for `artifact`. `getLogsForStep` reads only an invoked
+ * body's logs, the entry function's logs and the artifact's own logs; this is their union over every selector.
+ */
+export const artifactHasDebugLogs = (artifact: Artifact): boolean => {
+  const debug = artifact.debug;
+  if (debug === undefined) return false;
+  const hasLogs = (entry: { readonly logs?: readonly LogEntry[] }): boolean => (entry.logs?.length ?? 0) > 0;
+  return hasLogs(debug)
+    || Object.values(debug.functionDebug ?? {}).some(hasLogs)
+    || Object.values(debug.invokeDebug ?? {}).some(hasLogs);
+};
+```
+
+`Artifact` and `LogEntry` are already imported (`debugging.ts:14`). The optional `logs?` read tolerates an artifact
+loaded from JSON without the field. Covenant helper artifacts from `buildCovenantArtifact`
+(`packages/utils/src/state.ts:2744-2759`) have no `debug`, so they return false.
