+### 2d. `assertOperationCostDensity()` (new method; after `hasDebugLogs()`)
+
+```ts
+  /**
+   * Refuse a contract input over its BCH-2026 operation-cost budget, from one trace-free evaluation per contract
+   * input on the provider's VM. Every other build or evaluation failure is left to the later deciders. `standard`
+   * prices as the deciding VM does (SPEC S1): the provider's verifier on the plain path, the final preflight on the
+   * stateful path, which passes `true`.
+   */
+  assertOperationCostDensity(program?: LibauthProgram, standard = this.provider.policy?.enforceDust ?? true): void {
+    // Only BCH-2026 has a density rule; the debug this replaces evaluated under the provider's own target.
+    if (((this.provider as { vmTarget?: VmTarget }).vmTarget ?? DEFAULT_VM_TARGET) !== VmTarget.BCH_2026_05) return;
+    let evaluated: LibauthProgram;
+    try { evaluated = program ?? this.buildLibauthProgram(true); } catch { return; }
+    const vm = createVirtualMachineBch2026ForProvider(this.provider, undefined, { standard });
+    for (const [inputIndex, input] of this.inputs.entries()) {
+      if (!isContractUnlocker(input.unlocker)) continue;
+      let error: string | undefined;
+      try {
+        ({ error } = vm.evaluate({ inputIndex, ...evaluated }));
+      } catch { continue; }
+      if (!isOperationCostDensityError(error)) continue;
+      let bitauthUri = '';
+      try { bitauthUri = this.getSanitizedBitauthUri(); } catch { /* a custom unlocker has no template */ }
+      throw new FailedTransactionEvaluationError(
+        input.unlocker.contract.artifact, -1, inputIndex, bitauthUri, `${error}\n${OPERATION_COST_DENSITY_GUIDANCE}`,
+      );
+    }
+  }
+```
+
+Key logic and invariants:
+
+- **VM.** `createVirtualMachineBch2026ForProvider(this.provider, undefined, { standard })` with no observer returns
+  the per-provider cached VM for that regime (`network/createVirtualMachine.ts:948-968`). A provider with no
+  `consensusLimits` (every live network) gets stock libauth `createVirtualMachineBch2026(standard)`. A mock gets the
+  fast paths and enforces its published limits.
+- **Regime (SPEC S1).** On the plain path the default `standard` is the provider's verifier's own: `MockNetworkProvider`
+  builds its verifier with `standard: policy.enforceDust` on this same cached VM (`network/MockNetworkProvider.ts:380`,
+  `network/createPreparedTxVerifier.ts:65`), and live providers leave `policy` unset (`NetworkProvider.ts:65-66`), so
+  they price as a relaying node does. On the stateful path the decider is the final preflight, whose VM is standard
+  (`message-bus/preflight.ts:1127`, built with no options), and a prepared receipt lets the mock skip its own verify
+  (`network/createPreparedTxVerifier.ts:169`); the probe therefore passes `standard = true`.
+- **VM target.** The debug this replaces evaluated under the provider's target (`debugging.ts:60-75`;
+  `libauth-template/LibauthTemplate.ts:113-115`). The check runs only for BCH-2026 (`DEFAULT_VM_TARGET`,
+  `libauth-template/utils.ts:14`), so a `BCH_2023_05` mock, which has no density rule, refuses nothing new.
+- **Program.** With `program` given (plain path) there is no rebuild and no re-signing. Without it (stateful path)
+  the method builds once with `skipChecks = true`, the same as `_strictRecursiveVmPreflight`
+  (`stateful/StatefulTransactionBuilder.ts:7120`) and `_preflightRecursiveBuilder`. `sourceOutputs` is
+  `lastBuiltSourceOutputs` from that same build (`:1360-1365`), so it is not regenerated.
+- **Scope.** Contract inputs only (`isContractUnlocker`); P2PKH, placeholder and custom unlockers are skipped. All
+  contract inputs are evaluated, covenant or not, in input order; the first density failure throws.
+- **Failure behaviour.** The method throws only `FailedTransactionEvaluationError` for a density refusal. A build
+  exception, a JS exception inside `evaluate`, and every other VM error (require failure, NULLFAIL, non-truthy end)
+  are silent, exactly as the swallowed debug was. It never mutates the builder. `vm.evaluate` does not mutate the
+  program, so the encoded bytes are unaffected.
+- **Error.** The artifact is `input.unlocker.contract.artifact` (for a stateful covenant helper input, a
+  `DataNft_<cat8>`-style covenant artifact). `failingInstructionPointer` is -1 (D5). `bitauthUri` is computed only on
+  this failure path; it is the sanitized URI or '' when the template cannot be built (custom unlocker, or a failing
+  conservation check on a pre-fee build). Resulting message:
+  `Loop.scash Error in transaction at input 0 in contract Loop.scash.\nReason: Program attempted an operation that
+  would exceed the operation cost density limit. Maximum operation cost: ... \nThe budget is
+  operationCostBudgetPerByte x unlockingBytecodeLength, and for p2sh32 ... raises it.`
+
