+## 3. Stateful send probe
+
+### 3a. `stateful/stb-run-send-discovery-probe.ts` (rewrite lines 1-58)
+
+Current behaviour: at non-relaxed limits (`maximumInputBytes ?? 10_000` <= 10,000, so every live provider and the 10k
+mock) it runs `covenantBuilder.debug()`. A density error becomes a plain `Error` ("BCH-2026 operation-cost budget
+exceeded while probing the covenant ... Probe reported: ..."). Every other error goes to `console.debug` and is
+returned as `discoveryProbeFailure`, which the caller voids. It then always rebuilds.
+
+New file:
+
+```ts
+/**
+ * phase-boundary extract: STB send-phase extract - standard-limits send checks + post-discovery rebuild.
+ */
+
+import type { TransactionBuilder } from '../TransactionBuilder.js';
+
+export type DiscoveryProbeProvider = {
+  consensusLimits?: { maximumInputBytes?: number };
+};
+
+/**
+ * At standard limits, refuse a contract input over its operation-cost budget and print console.log output, then
+ * rebuild for fee measurement. The template debug only prints, so it runs only when an input's artifact has log
+ * entries, and its errors stay best-effort.
+ */
+export function runSendDiscoveryProbe(
+  covenantBuilder: TransactionBuilder,
+  provider: DiscoveryProbeProvider,
+  rebuild: () => TransactionBuilder,
+  sendTiming: (stage: string) => void,
+): { covenantBuilder: TransactionBuilder } {
+  sendTiming('initial-build');
+  // A relaxed mock may admit scripts hundreds of kilobytes long; its final preflight and verifier decide there.
+  const relaxedConsensus = (provider.consensusLimits?.maximumInputBytes ?? 10_000) > 10_000;
+  if (!relaxedConsensus) {
+    if (covenantBuilder.hasDebugLogs()) {
+      try { covenantBuilder.debug(); } catch (error) {
+        console.debug('STB debug() best-effort error:', error instanceof Error ? error.message : error);
+      }
+    }
+    // A density refusal cannot be repaired by the final signature, so it is the one outcome that throws. The final
+    // preflight decides this path and prices as standard (SPEC S1).
+    covenantBuilder.assertOperationCostDensity(undefined, true);
+  }
+
+  // Fee measurement and funding read this rebuilt shape; test/e2e/SendDebugGate.test.ts pins that the debug above
+  // does not change it.
+  const rebuilt = rebuild();
+  sendTiming('post-discovery-build');
+  return { covenantBuilder: rebuilt };
+}
+```
+
+- The header line 2 em-dash is replaced with ASCII " - ".
+- Ordering: the log-gated debug runs first, so logs print before a density refusal, as before. Then the density
+  check, then the rebuild. The density check uses the initial (pre-fee) build, as the old debug did.
+- `discoveryProbeFailure` is removed (dead: voided at the only call site).
+- Differences from today, all deliberate:
+  1. Error class: `Error` becomes `FailedTransactionEvaluationError`, and the message starts with
+     "<Name>.scash Error in transaction at input N..." instead of "BCH-2026 operation-cost budget exceeded while
+     probing...". The libauth sentence is kept.
+  2. Wider detection. The old probe saw a density failure only when it was the first failing input of a debuggable
+     template. It saw nothing when an earlier input failed first, when any input had a custom unlocker ("Cannot
+     debug..."), or when a conservation check failed in the template build. The new check evaluates every contract
+     input of the actual built transaction.
+  3. `console.debug` noise appears only for logging artifacts.
+- Sending timing stages are unchanged. `post-discovery-build` now measures density check + rebuild (+ debug when
+  the artifact logs), which is what the section 5.3 table should be re-measured against.
+
