+## 6. Memory item (b): fixed-point digest in `stateful/sc-derive-full-phase1-progressive-entries.ts`
+
+Current behaviour: `routeProbeTransactions` (`:121`) is a `Set<string>` of full transaction hex
+(`binToHex(encodeTransaction(tx))`) at `:125`, `:147` and `:226`. That is up to about 2.6 MB of string per pass on
+a mock-sized transaction. A repeated key means fixed point, so the loop breaks (`:227-234`).
+
+This lands with commit 3, not here. Commit 3 rewrites this loop (`spec/loops.md` section 7): `routeProbeTransactions`
+goes away, and its keys become the collector's admission candidates. Hashing only some keys would miss the fixed
+point and end in "Route probe convergence exhausted", so commit 3 keys every admission in the loop with one helper:
+
+```ts
+/** A fixed-point key for a built transaction: its encoding's digest, so each pass retains 64 characters. */
+const transactionKey = (transaction: Parameters<typeof encodeTransaction>[0]): string =>
+  binToHex(sha256Sync(encodeTransaction(transaction)));
+```
+
+Key equality is encoding equality up to a sha256 collision, so the decisions are today's. `encodeTransaction`,
+`binToHex` and `sha256 as sha256Sync` are already imported in that file. Commit 4 has nothing left in it.
